### In Plain Language *(illustrative only — §0–§14 below control if anything here reads differently)*

**Can anyone actually use and earn money from this, anywhere, right now? Yes, as a person — but not yet as a company, and read this first, because the honest answer has real teeth.** As of **14 September 2026**, according to the Custodian's own published research (the Jurisdictional Equality Status Table, §6.9.11), **zero of the 193 sovereign states on Earth have been determined TRUE — every single one starts out, and right now remains, UNKNOWN.** TRUE is never assumed, never automatic, and never granted by default; it is only ever shown, one jurisdiction at a time, through §6.9.2's test or §6.9.8's dossier process — and this is a snapshot, not a life sentence: it can and will change as jurisdictions are checked or reassessed. **Until at least one country gets there, no company, corporation, LLC, foundation, or any other legal entity may operate a product or service under this License at all — no compromise, no "least-bad available" jurisdiction to shelter in, not even for the Custodian's own SVE-Unicorns ventures.** That is the price of meaning it. But a real human being never needs a company to use this License — that was always true (§2) — so **a person, acting alone, in their own name, with their own unlimited personal liability and no corporate shield anywhere behind them, can build, run, and share this today, everywhere, TRUE or UNKNOWN.** They can always use it free for themselves. Ordinary wages and consulting fees for real work they actually do are never restricted, anywhere. And they can charge for what they build and keep the earnings — but only where that specific sale creates no tax bill for any UNKNOWN government; where it would, the same thing goes to that same person for free instead, never withheld. *"Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar's"* (Matthew 22:21) — nobody is asked to dodge their own personal taxes on what they honestly earn; what's off-limits is a transaction under this License being priced or routed so as to hand tax revenue to a government that cannot guarantee its own people's equal standing by birth, or any corporate structure feeding that government profit-shares, dividends, or a hosting footprint at all. **In short: people can always build and earn with this, on their own account, everywhere; companies wait for a country to earn TRUE first.**

**Can a government or a company itself be a customer, and does being generous buy you anything?** A person is served by default, everywhere, always — that never changes unless an audit later proves their own conduct produced bad fruit. A government or a company gets the opposite default: **nothing, by default — not free, not paid** — until two things both hold: first, its own jurisdiction's government has to formally commit to something concrete — give away 10% of whatever its institutions actually pay, plus a genuine share of its own know-how — training, mentorship, hands-on help — to one other jurisdiction, randomly and mutually matched, in a six-year teaching relationship followed by a seventh year of rest, then do it again with someone new (Indicator II, §6.9.16); and second, that specific institution has to itself be stood behind by one named, personally accountable human being, exactly as a company already needs a (God) Father just to operate this License at all. A non-profit school, library, or research institute keeps its own separate, unconditional free access regardless of any of this (§6.9.14(b)). Indicator II is entirely separate from, and cannot buy its way around, Indicator I's equality-by-birth test above: being generous doesn't excuse an amendable equality clause, and having an unamendable one doesn't excuse withholding reciprocity. Beneath both sits a third check, the Gate (§6.9.17, Indicator III): if a jurisdiction is shown — by an international or its own top court, a UN-level human-rights finding, or the firsthand, independent testimony of at least two real, identifiable, unconnected witnesses — to be suppressing a group's ethnicity, origin, religion, or language as a sustained pattern in everyday civic life, that finding zeroes out both of the other two indicators for as long as it stands, whatever either would otherwise show. A single incident, a lone accusation, or coordinated testimony dressed up as independent does not count. A jurisdiction not shown to fail the Gate is simply unaffected by it, the same way an unassessed jurisdiction is unaffected by Indicator I.

**Can a person keep their work secret for a while, the way a startup founder already can?** Yes. Founder Mode already lets a qualifying venture hold its methods back from publication until Year 44 if that's what surviving the market takes, without that counting as a breach — provided its fruits stay good and the work is hash-registered from day one so no one can later claim it wasn't SVE-bound all along. §4.9 gives an ordinary person, building alone, the same right — no size limit, no Year-44 ceiling, for as long as they live — if openness right now would put them in genuine danger, commercial, personal, or political. *"Do not give dogs what is holy, and do not throw your pearls before pigs, lest they trample them underfoot and turn to attack you"* (Matthew 7:6, Maxim III): this License asks for openness, not for someone to be thrown to whoever would only destroy them for it. The one absolute condition is death: everything must become fully open the moment the person holding it dies — no exceptions, no further secrecy, ever. Because sudden death can leave no one to carry that out, anyone using this is strongly urged to pre-schedule the release themselves — a timed, embargoed deposit (Zenodo's embargo feature, for one) that opens on its own on a fixed date, whether or not anyone else ever acts on it. None of this pauses the Fruits Test: bad fruit is still auditable at any time, in confidence, without forcing publication early — a freeze buys time, never a pass.

**What if even registering the freeze itself would be dangerous?** Then don't register it. Bunker Mode lets a person work with zero external trace at all — no registry entry, no announcement, nothing anyone outside their own trusted circle could ever notice — for as long as it takes to be safe, no later than death. The only cost is that nothing publicly proves when the work was really done until it's finally opened, which is why keeping a private, unpublished record of it (a hash told to no one, or held by a dead-man's-switch or a lawyer bound by confidentiality — never a public one) is strongly recommended instead of Zenodo's public embargo, which would itself give something away. *"For nothing is hidden that will not be made manifest, nor is anything secret that will not be known and come to light"* (Luke 8:17): this License trusts that on its own timeline, rather than force anyone to out themselves early to prove it. And if someone using Bunker Mode dies without ever opening it and without leaving any private record behind, there's nothing left to formally disclose — but whatever that work actually did in the world remains judged by its fruits regardless, exactly as this License has always judged everything else.

If you are new here: **you may use anything in the SVE Corpus — code, texts, ontologies, models, data — for any purpose, including to make money, without asking anyone first.** **Just touching, downloading, or running it already puts you inside this License — no signature required — and it makes no difference whether you got it from the official Registry or from someone who passed it along without authorization; a pirated copy binds you exactly like a licensed one, just as a pirated film doesn't exempt the viewer from copyright.** In exchange: **whatever you build with it has to stay just as open** — you cannot take a piece private, publish half and hide half, or wrap it in a closed product. **A product or service built on it must be open to every person on Earth, with zero exceptions for nationality, politics, or sanctions** — "the sun rises on the evil and the good" (Matthew 5:45), and so must you; the only lawful way to withhold it from one is to withhold it from everyone — and if you genuinely can't, there's no fallback license that lets you keep running it anyway while excluding them; you simply can't run it under this License there at all. **One more check, and it never costs a person anything.** Every country on Earth starts out UNKNOWN, none named, none exempt, until it's shown, not assumed, that some public equality clause — even just one line, no whole constitution required — guarantees everyone equal standing by birth regardless of ethnicity, descent, or religion (a ceremonial title like "Sir" or a hereditary honor doesn't count against this — only real legal rights do), and that not even that country's own parliament, courts, executive, or a referendum could ever touch that one line, through any process, ever. Short of that, the country stays UNKNOWN — but nobody there is denied the product or service over it: that would be exactly the kind of exclusion Universal Access already forbids. What actually happens for an UNKNOWN country is narrower and sharper: no server, office, or team may be based there, and not one payment under this License may be sent there, until it clears — everyone still gets served, from elsewhere, funded nowhere near it. An operator already lawfully set up in a country that turns out UNKNOWN gets a fair window to relocate and stop the payments, not an instant cutoff. **One more thing follows for UNKNOWN countries specifically: a person there can always use the product or service free, for themselves — but commercial terms (a price, a subscription, a fee) only work where they create zero tax bill for that country's own government.** If charging someone there would trigger even routine sales tax or VAT, the price simply isn't charged — there's nothing for that treasury to tax, because nothing is sold; ordinary wages paid to someone there for work they actually did are a different thing entirely and are never restricted by this. A non-profit school, library, or research institute physically there gets the same free access a person does. A country that clears the equality test gets ordinary commercial terms like everywhere else, subject to its own general law same as anywhere. Same question, same rule, same consequence, everywhere, for everyone. **Only a real human being can hold this License, full stop** — this office is called a **(God) Father** (read either word or both, your choice; it names a role, not a sex, gender, or religion — no faith is required to hold it). A company can use it, but only through one named (God) Father who is personally, permanently on the hook, with no corporate shield, and no court anywhere can read that requirement away: if a jurisdiction won't allow it, this License simply does not operate there at all, the same as Universal Access below. **Whoever uses the result is expected to use it for good** — bad fruit is grounds for the same audit as anything else. **If you do research, you must publish your field notes — successes and failures alike — and never fake a result**; investigators and journalists doing public-interest work get the same deal for free. **Training an AI model on this counts as building with it, too** — the model must be disclosed like any other derivative, and finding out later that it happened doesn't make it go away; it starts the clock on fixing it. **Reading it — even with a closed AI or a closed search engine — costs nothing and isn't restricted; the disclosure duty kicks in only once a system starts training on it or running on it, and from that point it applies the same way to everyone, closed or open.** **Your own private life is your own business, but the moment keeping something secret would mean hiding it from even one other person who's touched this Corpus through you — a client, an employer, a service's users — that isn't a smaller violation, it's a sign you shouldn't be using this Corpus at all.** **This License stands on its own** — even if a court somewhere throws out an earlier version, this one doesn't fall with it. **Even the Author's own earlier disclaimer of ownership doesn't undermine it: either the underlying authorship right was never waivable in the first place, or, if the disclaimer itself is invalid, everything reverts fully to the Author — both roads support this License.** **If your hands are clean, this License is almost frictionless; if they're not, every safeguard here applies at full strength and none of your past good conduct buys a discount** — that asymmetry is deliberate, and it's meant to correct, not merely punish. **Some uses are banned outright, no matter how much you pay or how transparent you are** — weapons, mass surveillance, deception at scale, harming children. And **if you ever accuse someone of breaking these rules, you go through the same check yourself, first.**

