### §0 — Continuity & Authority to Issue This Version
**0.1 Authority to issue.** Pending the SVE DAO or a functioning Veche, the Author & Initial Custodian (Dr. Artiom Kovnatsky) holds sole signature and publication rights under the **Declaration of Interim Custody v2.0**, exactly as already exercised for v5.0, v5.5, and the SVE-Unicorns Patch v1.0. v6.0 was drafted beginning 14 September 2026 and is planned for signature on **19 September 2026** (the Feast of the Miracle of the Archangel Michael at Chonae), God willing, by eIDAS/QES with OpenTimestamps confirmation — but signature and operative effect are deliberately not the same moment here. This version's **Effective Date** — the moment it actually becomes the operative SVE License, superseding v5.5 for Latent Activation by any new Recipient — is fixed separately, at **22 December 2026, 21:22 CET** (the winter solstice). Between signature and the Effective Date, v5.5 remains fully in force and continues to govern every new touch of the Corpus exactly as it does today; v6.0 exists in that interval as a signed, hash-locked, publicly disclosed text pending activation, not yet binding on anyone as the operative License. That interval is, in full, this version's public comment window — open from the moment of signature until the Effective Date, however many days that turns out to be, rather than a fixed count set in advance — during which anyone may submit a proposal, a correction, or a Jurisdictional Equality Dossier toward it exactly as if it were not yet finalized, because, operatively, it is not. The Custodian retains the right, at any point before the Effective Date, to withdraw this signed-but-pending text and replace it with a corrected version carrying forward the same or a new Effective Date; this is not a Ratchet violation and creates no reliance interest for anyone to disturb, because nothing has yet become operative for anyone to have relied on. Once the Effective Date passes without withdrawal, this text becomes irrevocably the operative License on the terms set out throughout it, and this withdrawal right lapses permanently, for this version, at that moment. Removing v5.0 §3's Non-Commercial fallback (see §10 below) was **not** a Ratchet violation when v5.5 did it, for the reasons already given there: NC was never among the immutable Core Principles, it directly conflicted with v4.0 §4/Appendix B's own Open Usage Right *and* with the SVE-Unicorns Patch's own requirement that Founder-Mode ventures be "a long-term, genuinely profitable business." **Elevating §2 (Natural-Person Rule) to non-severable status is likewise not a Ratchet violation — it is precisely the strengthening kind of change §13 reserves to the Custodian without needing a Veche**, because it only ever adds protection (a harder floor under personal accountability) and never removes one; v5.5's own §14 already put every reader on notice that this was a live, telegraphed possibility ("unless a future version elevates them — see the open questions in the drafting notes"), so this is the resolution of a question this framework asked of itself, not a new departure from it. **§6.9's Constitutional Equality Assurance is likewise a strengthening, not a narrowing, and so likewise not a Ratchet violation:** §6.2 already committed this License to Universal Access in absolute terms, and §6.9 does not touch that promise to persons at all — it adds a new, additional condition on *operators*, never on the people they serve: no jurisdiction that cannot keep its own equality-by-birth clause beyond the reach of its own legislature, courts, executive, or electorate may host this License's infrastructure or receive this License's money, but every person within it keeps exactly the access §6.2 already gave them. §6.9.9 keeps faith with §13's "no right already granted is diminished" promise directly: an operator already lawfully hosting infrastructure or remitting revenue in a jurisdiction that turns out to be UNKNOWN gets a fair transition window to relocate and stop remitting, not an instant, retroactive strike — and no end-user anywhere loses service on account of this section, ever.

**§6.9.14's Commercial-Use Ceiling is the same strengthening move again, aimed at the same target.** It does not touch §6.2's promise either: a natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction keeps full, free access for their own use, exactly as before — that floor never moves. What it adds is a new condition on *revenue*, not on *service*: a commercial (price-carrying) transaction with a person there is available only where it generates no tax payment to that jurisdiction's own government; where it would, the operator serves them free rather than not at all, which is strictly more access than an outright commercial denial would be, never less. An operator already lawfully charging natural persons in a jurisdiction that is or becomes UNKNOWN gets the same §6.9.9-style transition window before this applies to that arrangement, for the same reason given there.

**§6.9.15 is a strengthening too, not a weakening, even though it blocks every entity from operating under this License at all while zero jurisdictions are TRUE.** It resolves the same literal-reading problem §6.9.5 alone would otherwise create — that, applied to a world where every jurisdiction happens to be UNKNOWN at once, it would make lawful entity operation impossible everywhere simultaneously — but it resolves it by tightening the rule, not loosening it: rather than let an entity shelter anywhere on a "nothing is TRUE yet, so no rule can bind us" theory, §6.9.15(a) holds entities to no compromise at all, and accepts the consequence squarely — including that it reaches the Custodian's own SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode ventures exactly as it reaches anyone else's, per Radical Symmetry (§6.6). What it adds back is not a loophole for entities but a floor for persons: §6.9.15(b)–(c) confirm that a natural person's own direct, personally-liable exercise of §2.1 was never the "infrastructure" §6.9.5 meant to reach, so human beings are never left with nothing to do while jurisdictions are assessed — they may still build, run, and, at zero local tax, earn from what they build, entirely on their own account. No end-user loses anything on account of this section; the only thing suspended is a corporate shield's ability to operate at all before any jurisdiction has earned TRUE.

**§6.10 and §6.11 add nothing new in kind — they name explicitly what §6.2, §6.6, and §8.1 already implied, for the one class of decision where implication is not enough: who lives.** The Golden Rule (§6.10) is a restatement, not an expansion, of Radical Symmetry and Reciprocal-Audit-Priority — it changes no outcome those provisions did not already require, it only gives a name to the test being applied. §6.11 is that same principle's concrete floor for scarce, life-critical resources, sitting beside §6.1's Absolute Bars rather than beside §6.2's jurisdiction-facing Universal Access, because a scoring-by-utility harm reaches a person the same way regardless of which jurisdiction they are in, TRUE or UNKNOWN. Elevating §6.1, §6.10, and §6.11 to non-severable status (§14) closes a gap this text should have closed from the start — §6.1's Absolute Bars were never listed there — rather than opening a new one.

**§6.9.16's Parent–Child Reciprocity Program (Indicator II) and §6.9.17's Gate (Indicator III) are, again, strengthenings, not narrowings, for the same reason as everything else on this list: neither ever reduces what a natural person already receives under §6.2 or §6.9.14, and as of this draft's date zero jurisdictions have yet relied on unrestricted institutional access, so nothing already granted is taken back. §6.9.16 answers a question the original §6.9 text left open: whether a government or other institution within a jurisdiction may itself be charged for a Corpus-based product or service. Left unaddressed, that silence would have let a jurisdiction's own institutions buy in on ordinary commercial terms the moment it reached bare Indicator I TRUE, with nothing asked of it in return for the rest of the world; §6.9.16 closes that gap not by conditioning merely the commercial channel but by withholding the grant itself — the opposite default from a natural person's, and deliberately so. §6.9.19 makes explicit, as one cross-cutting rule, the asymmetry every part of this section already assumed: a natural person's access is the default this License protects, revocable only by an audit-proven bad-fruits finding; an entity's or institution's access is an earned exception to that default, on the same "almost frictionless for the compliant, uncompromising for the rest" logic §8.4 already states generally, and §6.2's promise to "every person and entity" is given its operative content by this Indicator exactly as it already is by §6.9.15's identical suspension of all entity operation, not weakened by either. Indicator I and Indicator II are deliberately kept independent and non-substitutable: generosity under the Reciprocity Program does not excuse an unamendable-equality failure, and an unamendable equality clause does not excuse withholding reciprocity — each is its own floor, and neither buys an exemption from the other. §6.9.17's Gate closes a different gap: §6.9.2 already tests only the formal text of a jurisdiction's law (§6.9.2(d)), which means a jurisdiction could satisfy Indicator I on paper while a documented pattern of ethnic, national, religious, ancestral, or linguistic suppression continues in its ordinary civic life underneath that text. The Gate does not lower §6.9.2's textual test or replace it; it adds beneath it exactly the same kind of substantive floor the Golden Rule (§6.10) and Scarce Resource Allocation (§6.11) already add elsewhere, and, consistent with this License's neutrality commitment (§6.9.0), it names no jurisdiction, people, or conflict anywhere in its own text — a finding under it depends entirely on documented fact, assessed jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction under §6.9.8's own non-partisan, no-self-certification process, never on this text's own characterization of any real-world situation.**

**§4.9's Human Quarantine is, once more, a strengthening rather than a narrowing, for a reason peculiar to this moment: §11's own freeze is currently inoperative for everyone, because §6.9.15(a) suspends all entity operation while zero jurisdictions are TRUE, and Founder Mode ventures are entities. Without §4.9, the freeze principle this License already accepts in §11 would have no natural person to attach to at all today — only a founder able to incorporate could ever use it, and no one can incorporate yet. §4.9 does not lengthen anyone's existing freeze or relax any of its conditions; it recognizes that the freeze's own justification — a real builder needs time before the world's scrutiny, or its predation, arrives — was never actually about entity form, and applies with at least equal force to a natural person building alone, who by definition already carries §11's full personal exposure. The one difference from §11 — no Year-44 ceiling — is balanced by a condition §11 does not have and does not need: because a natural person, unlike an entity, certainly dies, this subsection's own absolute backstop is stronger, not weaker, than a fixed year count could ever be. Maxim III is added to name, in Scripture, the judgment Founder Mode's freeze already made without naming it: this License asks for openness, but never demands that a sincere builder be handed over to those who would only trample the work and turn on its builder before either could be tested. §4.9(i)–(l)'s Bunker Mode closes one further gap in the same protection: registration itself, even hash-only and content-blind, is a visible act, and for a (God) Father in real danger, being seen to register anything can be exactly as costly as being seen to publish. Bunker Mode does not weaken this License's ultimate insistence on disclosure — the Bunker Opening remains due, absolutely, no later than death, on the same terms as any other freeze under this subsection — it only recognizes that the path to that disclosure must never itself require the one thing this whole subsection was written to prevent: putting a genuine builder in harm's way before their work, or their life, has run its course.**

**0.2 Standalone validity (independent of prior versions).** §0.1 explains why sole-signature issuance is legitimate as a matter of this framework's own internal governance — but this License's validity does not ultimately depend on that story at all. It derives directly and independently from the Author's own, original, unalienated authorship and copyright in the Corpus Artifacts as their sole creator, not from the validity of v1.3, v4.0, v5.0, v5.5, or the SVE-Unicorns Patch v1.0. Those instruments are cited here for continuity, historical record, and the Ratchet Principle's comparison baseline — never as this License's source of authority. If any prior version, or any provision of one, is anywhere held invalid, unenforceable, procedurally defective, or improperly issued, that holding does not affect, impair, or in any way taint this License: v6.0 stands as a fresh, self-sufficient grant and unilateral covenant in its own right, wherever necessary severable in its entire validity from the fate of any predecessor instrument.

This standalone footing is not disturbed by the Author's own disclaimer of "ownership rights" under the Declaration of Interim Custody v2.0 §§2, 5a, which states the Author "retains no ownership rights — only authorship and the duty to safeguard methodological integrity." That disclaimer renounces proprietary, exclusive, for-profit ownership — holding the Corpus as closed private property — not the underlying personal authorship itself. In many jurisdictions (for example, Germany, UrhG §§11–14; Estonia, AutÕS §12; France's *droit moral* tradition) an author's moral rights — authorship, integrity, and the right to determine the terms on which a work is first communicated to the public — are inalienable by law and cannot be waived even by the author's own declaration; a purported waiver of them is void to that extent, and the underlying rights persist and continue to support this License regardless of what the disclaimer accomplishes as to ownership. Where a jurisdiction does not recognize inalienable moral rights of this kind — this varies, see "Left for Counsel" in the companion document — the same question resolves the same way from the other direction: if the ownership disclaimer is instead held invalid or ineffective there, the disclaimed rights revert to the Author as sole original rightsholder, which independently supports this License under ordinary copyright, without reliance on the custodial framework at all. Either branch validates v6.0; there is no branch that does not.

**0.3 Contributions carry no veto.** Anyone who submits a contribution, fix, comment, pull request, or similar input toward the Corpus or this License thereby grants the Custodian, irrevocably and unconditionally, a perpetual, worldwide license — and, to the extent the contribution is itself copyrightable, an assignment — sufficient to incorporate it under SVE terms. This applies whether the contributor is a natural person or submits on behalf of an entity: accepting a contribution is not the same as that party holding a license under §2, and creates no (God) Father requirement. Submitting a contribution does not confer co-authorship of this License, a veto over its governance, or any right to demand its withdrawal, amendment, or non-distribution — governance and amendment remain governed solely by §0.1 above and, once constituted, the Veche.

**0.4 Tool & Synthesizer Independence.** Formulating, drafting, refining, or proofreading a Corpus Artifact with the assistance of an interactive software tool, computational assistant, language model, or compiler — regardless of provider — conveys no proprietary interest in that Artifact to the tool's developer or operator. Under the ordinary terms of service such providers themselves publish, rights in a user's inputs and the resulting outputs vest in the user; the architecture, synthesis, selection, and final verification remain the Author's own original work, exactly as they would using a word processor or a compiler. A tool provider who later claims to have derived, trained on, or discovered a Corpus Artifact through its own records of an Author-tool interaction — rather than through the Registry — does not thereby escape this License, which reaches an Artifact through any channel, direct or intermediary (§1.3, §4.5); such a claim is, if anything, an admission of direct copying from an identified source, and may separately implicate that provider's own data-handling commitments or confidentiality obligations under applicable law — matters this License neither creates nor waives.

### §1 — Scope (Cinema Clause)
**1.1 Objective coverage.** Coverage is objective: every Artifact — code, texts, ontologies, schemas, models, data, architectural specifications — is in scope the moment its hash is timestamped in the Prior-Art registry (**https://zenodo.org/communities/sve**), including Artifacts registered after this License. This License governs the *distribution* of that expression — copying, adapting, running as a service — exactly as a film license governs prints and screenings, not the story. It does not claim rights copyright cannot give (bare ideas, methods, "phenomena of reality... not mentioned at all," as v5.0 §1 overreached); an undocumented idea is protected instead by Defensive Publication (§7).

**1.2 Latent Activation — click, touch, or use is consent.** This License is a unilateral public grant, not a negotiated bilateral contract: there is no counterparty to sign with, and none is needed. Rights and obligations attach the instant a person downloads, reads, runs, modifies, forwards, or offers as a Network Service any Corpus Artifact — whichever comes first — not upon signature, registration, account creation, or payment. Where an official Custodian channel presents an explicit accept-or-click step, that click is simply the clearest evidence of what Latent Activation already accomplishes; its absence changes nothing. This is Core Principle 4 of Meta-License v4.0 (Latent Activation), made explicit and operative here, with the same legal ancestry v4.0's own Legal Ancestors table already cites: clickwrap enforceability (*ProCD, Inc. v. Zeidenberg*, 86 F.3d 1447 (7th Cir. 1996)) and GPL-style copyleft, which binds on use, not on signature.

**1.3 Channel independence — the Cinema Clause applied to piracy.** Because §1.1 makes coverage a fact about the Artifact's hash, not about how a given copy reached a given Recipient, obtaining a Corpus Artifact through an unauthorized, unofficial, or "pirate" channel — a mirror, a forward, a third-party repost, a leak — does **not** exempt the Recipient from this License. It places them inside it, on identical terms to a Recipient who obtained it from the Registry directly: exactly as watching a pirated copy of a film does not exempt the viewer from copyright, or grant them any right the licensed viewer lacks. A party who strips or omits required Provenance notices (§4.3) is independently liable for that breach; stripping notices does not free anyone further downstream — the Registry's public, hash-addressable record stands as constructive notice regardless, on the same footing as a patent register. There is no clean-hands exit from this License through an unofficial copy; there is only compliance or breach.

### §2 — Who May Hold This License (Natural-Person Rule)
**2.0 The office of (God) Father.** Every natural person who holds this License directly under §2.1, or who personally sponsors and answers for a legal entity's exercise of it under §2.2, holds the title **(God) Father** — the sole office this License recognizes as capable of receiving or exercising rights under §3. Read it as "Father" or as "Godfather," at the reader's own choice; both readings name the identical office and carry identical force. The title names an office, not a sex, gender, or gender identity: it is held on exactly the same terms, with exactly the same weight, by every (God) Father regardless of who they are — exactly as "Custodian" already denotes an office rather than a person's characteristics, not a role reserved to one sex. It carries no religious qualification of any kind: holding it requires no faith, belief, creed, practice, or affiliation, and no one may be refused or removed from the office on that basis — "God" in the title reflects only this License's own stated framing (§0's Maxims, Matthew 5:45, the Symbolic Witness at the close of the companion document), never a test applied to who may hold it. Only a natural person who has reached the age of majority and full legal capacity under the law applicable to them may hold this office; where the benefit of a Corpus Artifact is meant to reach a minor or a person without full legal capacity, an adult (God) Father holds the office on their behalf, per ordinary guardianship or representation principles in that jurisdiction. Wherever this License, its Appendices, or a predecessor version uses "Sponsor," that term is fully synonymous with (God) Father; the title carries no substantive change to this section's duties, only a name.

**2.1** Only a natural person — a living human being — may be a Recipient under §3 and exercise rights directly under this License, holding the office of (God) Father while doing so. A legal entity (corporation, LLC, partnership, foundation, government body, trust, DAO treasury, or similar) cannot itself hold, receive, or exercise rights under this License.

**2.2 Operating through an entity.** A legal entity may still build and operate a product or service on Corpus Artifacts, but only through at least one specific, named natural person (a **(God) Father**) who personally accepts this License in their own name and remains personally, individually, and without limitation liable for that entity's compliance — audited, terminated, and subject to Appendix F consequences in their own name, regardless of any corporate or limited-liability shield. Where more than one (God) Father is named for the same entity, each holds full, undivided, personal liability — never shared out or diluted among them; each is independently and completely answerable, exactly as if they were the only one. If a (God) Father departs, dies, or is removed, the entity must name a successor within 90 days or its grant lapses.

**2.3 Outside SVE.** This does not touch the entity's ordinary contracts, corporate structure, or limited liability for anything *outside* this License — a company remains free to organize itself however it likes. It simply cannot use that structure to place its SVE compliance behind a wall no one is personally answerable for. A closed circle of liability is itself a form of enclosure (§5).

**2.4 No Shield of Any Kind.** A (God) Father must be a real, reachable, personally exposed human being — not merely a named one. A (God) Father may act under a pseudonym only if that pseudonym is traceable, on the same terms as any other Recipient under §8's audit, to a real, accountable person — an unreachable or purely anonymous (God) Father is no (God) Father, and the grant does not attach. The same follows, for the same reason, wherever the named individual: **(a)** holds head-of-state, head-of-government, diplomatic, parliamentary, judicial, sovereign, or other official or public immunity — under any legal system, domestic or international — that would bar, limit, or functionally prevent a court or tribunal from holding them personally, individually, and without limitation liable for the entity's SVE compliance, unless that immunity has been validly, effectively, and irrevocably waived, in a form recognized by the law that would otherwise grant it, before the grant attaches and for its full duration; a waiver that is nominal but not practically enforceable — because no forum genuinely capable of entering and enforcing a personal judgment against them actually exists, or because it is not independent of the very government or entity the immunity would otherwise protect — does not satisfy this section; **(b)** is named on paper but does not, in fact, exercise or have the practical authority to exercise real decision-making control over the entity's compliance with this License — a nominal, figurehead, or "straw" (God) Father with no actual control is treated identically to an anonymous one; or **(c)** is indemnified, insured, reimbursed, or otherwise made whole by the entity or any third party for any liability, penalty, or consequence this License imposes on them personally — an arrangement that quietly restores the corporate shield §2.2 forecloses is no less a shield for being informal, private, or undisclosed. Whether such an immunity, arrangement, or lack of real control exists, and whether it has been effectively removed, is itself an ordinary question for §8's suspicion-triggered audit. Where sovereign or official immunity cannot, as a matter of the relevant jurisdiction's own law, ever be waived by the individual who holds it, the result is the one §2.7 already provides for any other unenforceable case: the office does not attach there for that individual, and no grant subsists for that product or service under this License.

**2.5 Payment is not licensure.** A legal entity — including the SVE Foundation, a community treasury, or a payment processor — may still receive funds under §10's revenue-share without itself being a Recipient: accepting money is not exercising rights under §3.

**2.6 Not the SVE governance apparatus.** This section governs Recipients — those receiving and exercising rights under §3. It does not require the Custodian, the Veche, the DVN, the SVE Foundation, or other SVE governance bodies to name a (God) Father for their own governance functions; it governs who may *use* the Corpus, not the bodies that steward it. This includes the Custodian's own ventures: per §6.6, Radical Symmetry means the Custodian binds himself first, and when the Custodian personally operates a product or service under this License, he holds the office of (God) Father on identical terms to anyone else — no exemption, no special case.

**2.7 Non-severable — and no fallback substitute.** Because the Natural-Person Rule, and the office of (God) Father it defines, is this License's structural precondition for personal accountability — the identified human being through whom every other duty in this License (disclosure, revenue-share, audit, and Appendix F's betrayal consequences) is ultimately enforced — §2.1–§2.4 stand on the same non-severable footing as §0, the Core Principles, and §6.2–§6.5. No court may narrow them piecemeal, read them down to permit direct entity licensure, or substitute a lesser accountability mechanism (a compliance officer, a named legal representative without personal exposure, corporate officer liability alone) for the natural person this section requires. If held unenforceable somewhere, the remainder is read to maximize alignment with it; only if that is impossible does this License become void in that jurisdiction — see §14. That voidance is contained to that jurisdiction only (§0.2). Within it, the Dormant Sliding Fallback (§12) does not reach §2, at any rung, for that product or service — exactly as it already does not reach §6 or §8 — no AGPL, no CC BY-SA, nothing stands in for the natural person this License requires. §6.3's logic governs the practical consequence: no grant of any kind subsists for a product or service that cannot satisfy this section where it operates. A legal entity is not a substitute rightsholder merely because a jurisdiction will not recognize the alternative. Personal accountability is not a copyright condition to be downgraded; alongside human dignity (§6.7), it is part of the floor everything else stands on.

### §3 — Grant
Each Recipient receives a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license, continuing during compliance, to reproduce, distribute, adapt, and run as a Network Service any Corpus Artifact — **in any field of endeavor, including commercial use, without prior authorization** — subject to §§4–10.

### §4 — Anti-Enclosure (Share-Alike / Network Copyleft)
**4.1** Distribute or adapt only under this License; no additional restriction, no relicensing into closed terms.

**4.2 Network Service disclosure.** Whoever runs a Network Service materially relying on a Corpus Artifact must make available to that Service's users the corresponding modifications — source code for software; full schemas, ontologies, parameters, and model weights for non-code Artifacts.

**4.3 Provenance notices.** Every copy or redistribution, official or not, must preserve the Artifact's License reference, its Registry hash, and a link to **https://zenodo.org/communities/sve**. A party who strips, alters, or omits these notices is independently liable for that breach (§8), and gains no shelter from it — it does not free anyone further downstream from this License (see §1.3).

**4.4** No technical or contractual measure may defeat any of §§4.1–4.3.

**4.5 AI training is adaptation; TDM exception opted out.** Using a Corpus Artifact — in whole or in part, alone or blended with other material — to train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise derive the parameters of a machine-learning model is an adaptation under §4.1 and creates a Derivative, triggering §4.2's disclosure duty (full parameters/weights) regardless of whether any individual weight can be isolated or "traced back" to a specific input: neural-network weight entanglement is not a defense to Derivative status. What matters is inclusion of the Artifact in the training process, not extractability of the output. The Author expressly opts out, to the maximum extent permitted, of any Text-and-Data-Mining exception that would otherwise permit this without a license — including under Article 4 of EU Directive 2019/790 — exercising the Article 4(3) reservation mechanism; this reservation is expressed in this text and, where technically supported, in machine-readable form at the Registry. A Recipient's own internal characterization of the use — "research only," "safety testing," "not production," a log entry describing limited use — does not itself exempt that use from this section where the objective fact of training-data inclusion is established by any evidence: the Recipient's own records, a dataset manifest, third-party disclosure, or demonstrated model behavior. §1.3's channel-independence rule applies identically here: an Artifact that reached a training corpus indirectly — via a third-party dataset, a scrape-of-a-scrape, or an intermediary redistributor — does not escape coverage. This section reflects a principle wider than any one Artifact: a system that already draws on humanity's collective intellectual output owes reciprocal openness in equal measure — the Corpus is simply the hash-verifiable instance of that principle this License can enforce directly.

**4.6 Discovery duty.** A Recipient who discovers — through their own logs, an internal audit, external research, or otherwise — that a Corpus Artifact was used, directly or via an intermediary, in training a model they still operate or distribute, must bring that product or service into compliance with this License (disclosure, revenue-share, and all other applicable duties) from the date of discovery forward. Continuing to operate without disclosing a known prior inclusion is concealment; concealment after discovery is independently a Fruits Test breach auditable under §8, regardless of whether the original training predates this License.

**4.7 No Secondary Secrecy.** Maxim II ("live by your skills and talents — not by your secrets") is operative, not decorative. A Recipient's own private matters — what they alone know, touching no other person's use of a Corpus Artifact — are entirely outside this License's reach: privacy is not enclosure, and nothing here asks anyone to live without one. The line sits exactly where a second party enters the picture: the moment a Corpus Artifact is used, built on, modified, or operated in a way that involves anyone beyond the Recipient's own person — an employer, a client, a Service's users, a counterparty, a collaborator — the transparency §§4.1–4.6 and §5 already require applies in full; there is no "confidential" or "NDA-protected" tier of SVE use, and dressing enclosure up as a business-confidentiality term is not a lesser violation. A Recipient or (God) Father who needs standing secrecy toward another party about what a Corpus Artifact is, does, or was used for should not use the Corpus at all — that need is itself incompatible with this License, not a lesser breach of it.

This does not forbid ordinary, disclosed, time-bound collaboration: coworkers and contractors building something together ahead of a scheduled, registered disclosure — including under SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode's freeze (§11) — are not "secondary secrecy" in the sense this section targets; the target is secrecy that serves enclosure, a permanent or indefinite wall against the outside world, not the ordinary process of building something with other people before telling everyone else. Nor does it reach a party's confidentiality about matters genuinely unrelated to a Corpus Artifact's use (an unrelated vendor NDA, unrelated trade secrets, an employee's compensation), or privileged legal advice about how to comply with this License — consulting counsel about SVE obligations privileges the analysis, not the underlying Corpus-touching facts, which remain fully disclosable. Where secrecy is not chosen but legally compelled — a court seal, a gag order, a lawful government demand — §6.3's withdrawal logic applies by analogy: continuing to operate the affected product or service under this License while concealing what compliance requires disclosing is not permitted, but withdrawing it from this License for the duration of the compulsion is. Protecting personal data or a vulnerable individual's privacy (§9.5) is never "secrecy" in the sense this section forbids — it protects a person, not an enclosure.

**4.8 Reading is free; incorporation is not — no status-based exception.** Nothing in this License restricts who may read, study, index, or discuss a Corpus Artifact: a closed-source AI system, a proprietary search engine, or any other party may inspect it exactly as any human reader may, without triggering any duty — ideas and inspection remain free under §1.1, and Universal Access (§6.2) admits no exception for anyone, closed-source companies included; this section adds no new exception either. What §4.5 regulates is not who looks, but what happens next: a system — open or closed — that trains on, fine-tunes with, or otherwise incorporates a Corpus Artifact into its operative parameters, while keeping the resulting parameters closed, is in the same full, uncured breach of §4.2/§4.5 as any other undisclosed derivative; there is no separate, lesser "closed-use" tier, and no discount for size or market position. A closed system cannot, as a practical matter, train on the Corpus and remain closed for that part without breaching this License — but that is the ordinary disclosure duty applying symmetrically to everyone, the same way it always has, not a new carve-out into §6.2 aimed at anyone in particular. Indexing, by any search engine regardless of its own licensing model, is not itself an adaptation and needs no license; only a synthesis or answer feature built from indexed Corpus content that materially relies on it is a Network Service under §4.2, subject to the same disclosure duty as any other derivative.

**4.9 Human Quarantine — the Founder Mode freeze, extended to any natural person, ended only by death.** §11's SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode already lets a qualifying venture *freeze* — defer publication of — its methods until Year 44 without that freeze counting as enclosure, provided good fruits hold and the work is hash-registered as SVE-bound from day one. This subsection extends the same principle, without Founder Mode's size thresholds or its Year-44 ceiling, to any (God) Father acting directly under §2.1: where disclosure would expose that person to genuine danger — commercial predation before their own work can stand on its own feet, personal or political retaliation, or a comparable real threat — they may likewise freeze disclosure of a Corpus-based Artifact they have built, for as long as they live. *"Do not give dogs what is holy, and do not throw your pearls before pigs, lest they trample them underfoot and turn to attack you."* — Matthew 7:6 (Maxim III). This is not a license to live by secrets (Maxim II): it is a recognition that timing, not permanence, is what Maxim II actually asks for, and this subsection's one absolute condition makes that timing finite for everyone, without exception.

**(a) Registration from day one.** A frozen Artifact must be hash-registered at the Registry as SVE-bound at or near the time of its creation, exactly as §11 already requires of Founder Mode — provenance and priority are preserved and publicly timestamped even while the content itself stays embargoed; a claimed freeze over work not so registered when created is not a freeze this subsection recognizes, and is an ordinary, uncured §4 breach. Where even this registration would itself endanger the (God) Father, (i) below governs instead of this subsection.

**(b) Natural persons only; entities keep their own, separate freeze.** This subsection is available only to a natural person acting directly under §2.1 — it does not extend to an entity operating under §2.2, which remains bound by §11's own, size-thresholded, Year-44-capped freeze (itself currently suspended in its own operation by §6.9.15 while zero jurisdictions are TRUE — which makes this subsection, today, the only freeze mechanism actually available to anyone). A (God) Father who later incorporates a frozen work into a Founder Mode venture, once that becomes possible, carries this subsection's own registration date forward until conversion, exactly as §6.9.15(e) already provides for a comparable transition.

**(c) The one absolute condition: full disclosure on death.** A natural person's Human Quarantine ends, without exception and without further notice, the moment they die. From that moment, every Artifact they held under this subsection must become fully disclosed and freely available under this License — the same disclosure §4.2, §4.5, and §9.2 would have required all along, simply deferred, never waived. Nothing in this subsection authorizes secrecy that outlives the person who held it; where the (God) Father dies, whoever then holds, controls, or inherits the frozen material — an heir, an executor, an estate, or anyone else in possession of it — takes it subject to this same disclosure duty, exactly as they would take it subject to any other obligation attaching to property they inherit.

**(d) Strongly recommended: time-capsule registration.** Because a sudden or unexpected death can leave no one both willing and able to carry out (c), a (God) Father using this subsection is strongly encouraged — though not required — to pre-register a scheduled, embargoed public release for each frozen Artifact during their own lifetime, set to open automatically on a fixed future date regardless of anyone's later action (for example, a Zenodo deposit under a time-limited access embargo). A self-executing, pre-scheduled release of this kind discharges (c) on its own terms without depending on any survivor's cooperation, and is the most reliable way to honor this subsection's one absolute condition; a (God) Father who declines to set one should expect an audit under (f) to weigh that absence, among everything else, in judging whether a claimed freeze is made in good faith. An embargo date set so far out that it is not a realistic estimate of the (God) Father's own remaining lifetime, or left unrenewed well past a reasonable planning horizon, is treated the same way.

**(e) Good fruits, in full, the entire time.** Freezing disclosure never freezes §8's Fruits Test: a (God) Father exercising this subsection remains bound by the Fruits Test, §6.1's Absolute Bars, and every other duty of this License exactly as if disclosure were not deferred at all. §6.1 in particular is never shielded by a freeze under this subsection, on the same non-severable, no-cure terms it already carries everywhere else in this License.

**(f) Audited on suspicion, in full, without defeating the freeze.** A frozen Artifact is fully subject to §8's suspicion-triggered audit at any time, exactly as a Founder Mode venture already is under §11 — a freeze defers *public* disclosure; it never defers *accountability*. Where suspicion is raised, the (God) Father must submit the frozen material for confidential review by the Custodian, or a comparably independent, confidentiality-bound reviewer the Custodian designates, sufficient to determine compliance with §6.1 and the Fruits Test without itself publishing what remains embargoed; refusing that confidential review is treated as §8.4 already treats refusing any other properly-initiated audit — as supplying the adverse evidence itself, and grounds to terminate the freeze and require immediate disclosure.

**(g) What a freeze does not touch.** This subsection defers disclosure alone. It does not defer, reduce, or excuse §10's ordinary revenue-share obligation, §6.9's jurisdiction-based conditions, or §2.4's requirement that the (God) Father themselves remain a real, traceable, accountable person — Human Quarantine hides what was built and how, never who built it. Nor does it override §9.5's protection for a confidential source or a vulnerable third party whose safety depends on it: the disclosure due under (c) is of the (God) Father's own work, not of another person's protected identity within it.

**(h) No workaround.** §6.9.7's no-workaround logic applies here in full: an entity may not route its own work through a nominally independent natural person to claim this subsection's uncapped, death-triggered terms in place of §11's own, narrower freeze; doing so is a workaround, independently auditable under §8, and treated as an ordinary entity operation for every purpose this License cares about, including §6.9.15. This applies with at least equal force to (i) below: the absence of a registry trail is never a reason to relax it, and a disguised entity caught operating through Bunker Mode after the fact gains no discount under §8.4 for however long the absence of any trail let it go unnoticed.

**(i) Bunker Mode — zero external trace, for the most hostile environments.** Even a hash-registered, publicly-timestamped freeze under (a) can itself be dangerous: the bare fact that someone has registered *something*, however little it reveals, can be exactly the signal that invites the attack, investigation, or retaliation this whole subsection exists to prevent. Where that is a real risk, a (God) Father may instead build, hold, and fully comply with this License entirely offline, with no registration at the Registry and no trace of any kind anywhere visible to anyone outside their own trusted circle — not a filing, not a public announcement, not a single word — until they themselves choose to disclose it (the "Bunker Opening"), on the same absolute, no-later-than-death terms (c) already sets. This License never requires a person to create a visible record of their own danger merely to remain in good standing under it; where safety and the ordinary registration step in (a) conflict, safety governs, and choosing this subsection over (a) is not itself a breach of anything, nor evidence of one.

**(j) What Bunker Mode costs, and how to offset it privately.** A Bunker Mode Artifact carries none of the Registry's public priority protection until the Bunker Opening: this License cannot prove, to anyone outside the (God) Father's own trusted circle, when the work was actually created until it is disclosed, and using this subsection means accepting that trade-off knowingly in exchange for complete invisibility in the meantime. In (d)'s place — a public, pre-scheduled embargoed deposit is itself a visible trace, and defeats the purpose of this subsection — a (God) Father here is strongly encouraged to keep a private equivalent instead: computing and privately retaining a hash of the work using the same method the Registry itself uses, told to no one, or entrusted only to a small number of deeply trusted people, a dead-man's-switch service, or an attorney bound by privilege, configured to release the material if the (God) Father does not periodically confirm they are still able to hold it — without that arrangement itself ever being visible to anyone outside it. At the Bunker Opening, revealing the material together with a hash that already existed beforehand proves the timing was genuine, without that hash ever having been public before that moment. None of this is required, for the same reason (d) is not required of ordinary Quarantine — but its absence leaves (c)'s promise resting entirely on what survives the (God) Father, which is precisely the risk this subsection exists to reduce.

**(k) If the bunker is never opened.** Where a (God) Father dies without opening the bunker and without leaving any surviving private record — the risk (j) exists to reduce, not eliminate — this License cannot compel disclosure of a work it has no way to know exists; that is a structural limit on any accountability mechanism, not a loophole this subsection creates. What does not lapse is the Fruits Test's own substance (§8.1; Matthew 7:16–20, "you will know them by their fruits"): a Bunker Mode work that has already had real effects in the world remains judged by those effects, observable independently of any disclosed methodology, exactly as the Fruits Test has always judged — by what a work has actually done, not only by what a court can compel someone to show. Nothing here excuses bad fruit merely because its origin was never disclosed, and if suspicion of bad fruit arises from a Bunker Mode work's own visible effects — even with its builder unidentified or unreachable — §8's audit applies to whatever and whoever can still be reached, exactly as it would to any other suspected breach.

**(l) Priority: the Human, first.** *"For nothing is hidden that will not be made manifest, nor is anything secret that will not be known and come to light."* — Luke 8:17. Where anything else in this section would otherwise force a choice between the (God) Father's own safety and strict compliance with a formality — timing of registration, form of notice, or any comparable step — that choice resolves in the Human's favor, here and throughout §4.9. This License trusts that principle to hold in its own time rather than forcing a person to disclose themselves into danger to prove it early; it asks only that, when it is safe to do so, and no later than death, the truth is finally let out.

### §5 — Wholeness Clause (No Partial Enclosure)
You may not take one part of the Corpus (say, an ontology) open while keeping what you built on top of it closed, or vice versa — the obligations of §4 attach to the whole integrated work. Nor may you accept the grant of §3 while declining the conditions of §§4–10: the two are one instrument, and partial acceptance is void. A breach here is a One-Bit violation (Appendix F §1 of Meta-License v4.0) — immediate termination.

### §6 — Ethical-Use Floor & Universal Access (Radical Symmetry)
**6.1 Absolute bars.** No tier, payment, or transparency log cures the following — void *ab initio* regardless of any other term: **(a)** lethal autonomous weapons or targeting systems; **(b)** mass covert surveillance or repression without due process; **(c)** disinformation or psychological-manipulation campaigns at scale; **(d)** any exploitation of minors.

**6.2 Universal Access — absolute.** A product or service built on a Corpus Artifact must be offered on the same terms to every person and entity on Earth. **No exception** for nationality, citizenship, geography, political affiliation, sanctions status, government designation, or religion. *"He makes His sun rise on the evil and on the good, and sends rain on the just and on the unjust."* — Matthew 5:45. This License claims no lesser standard, and none is read into it. This gives absolute, unconditional operative force to Commandment 6 of the SVE-Unicorns Patch and to Core Principle 2, Radical Symmetry (Meta-License v4.0 §2.2).

**6.3 No selective withdrawal.** This License has no power to instruct anyone to break a law that actually binds them, and does not try. What it does not permit is *selective* compliance: serving some and withholding from others while continuing to operate the same product or service under this License. An operator who cannot lawfully serve everyone under §6.2 has exactly one path that keeps this License in force: **withdraw that product or service from this License entirely, for everyone, for as long as the conflict stands** — never carve out the forbidden party while keeping the rest of the market. Serving everyone but one is a §6.2 breach. Serving no one under SVE terms is not.

**6.4 Conduct, not identity.** §6.2 bars turning someone away for *who they are*. It does not protect *what they do*: an operator may suspend a specific user for confirmed bad-fruits conduct under §8.2, following the same audit-first sequencing as §8.3. That is a conduct-based distinction, not a status-based one, and does not implicate this section — Matthew 5:45's symmetry governs standing to receive, not license to harm.

**6.5 Transparency & audit.** Any withdrawal under §6.3 must be publicly logged (what, why, since when) and is subject to §8's Reciprocal-Audit-Priority rule on challenge. A claimed §6.3 withdrawal that turns out to still be serving some users while excluding others is the §6.2 breach it actually is — not a lesser matter.

**6.6 Symmetry cuts both ways.** §6.2–6.5 bind identically no matter whose politics or sanctions are at issue, and identically to the Custodian's own ventures, including any under SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode — Radical Symmetry means the Custodian binds himself first.

**6.7 Non-severable — and no fallback substitute.** Because §6.2 restates Core Principle 2 (Radical Symmetry), which Meta-License v4.0 §2 makes immutable, §6.2–§6.5 stand on the same non-severable footing as §0 and the Core Principles: no court may narrow them piecemeal. If held unenforceable somewhere, the remainder is read to maximize alignment with them; only if that is impossible does this License become void in that jurisdiction — see §14. That voidance, where it occurs, is contained to that jurisdiction only, not spread worldwide (§0.2's standalone-validity principle runs equally in this direction). But within that jurisdiction, there is no consolation prize: the Dormant Sliding Fallback (§12) does **not** reach §6, at any rung, for that product or service. A fallback that let an operator keep operating on lesser terms while still excluding whoever the local restriction targets would itself be exactly the selective compliance §6.3 already forbids, arrived at through a side door. If a given product or service cannot honor §6 in a given jurisdiction, no grant of any kind — primary or fallback — subsists there for it: not AGPL, not CC BY-SA, nothing. §6.3's own all-or-nothing withdrawal remains the only lawful way back in. Human dignity is not a copyright condition to be downgraded; it is the floor everything else stands on.

**6.8 Consequence.** A breach of §6.1 or §6.2 is an Appendix F betrayal case: immediate termination of all rights under this License, no cure, no repentance path.

**6.9 Constitutional Equality Assurance — one clause, absolutely unamendable; UNKNOWN jurisdictions: everyone served, nothing hosted there, nothing paid there.**

**6.9.0 Purpose, neutrality, and provenance.** This section gives operative, verifiable content to §6.2's promise that this License's grant does not make the Custodian, a Recipient, or a (God) Father complicit in a legal order that itself denies the equal standing of human beings by birth — while keeping Matthew 5:45's symmetry intact for the people of every jurisdiction, however their own state is classified. It names no country, people, or religion, anywhere in its text or in any application of it, and applies one identical rule, one identical evidentiary standard, and one identical consequence to every sovereign jurisdiction, sub-national unit, and other territory on Earth in which a product or service under this License is offered, hosted, operated, or materially relied upon — including the Custodian's own (§6.6). Earlier working drafts toward this License, and materials independently produced by other drafting tools along the way, explored several shapes of this mechanism: one addressed to a single named jurisdiction; later ones generalized to no jurisdiction but built around an elaborate, multi-element "Qualifying Constitution" test and a full territorial block on an unproven jurisdiction. This section supersedes and replaces every such draft in its entirety, simplifying the test to the one thing that actually matters — whether the equality guarantee can be touched by anyone, ever, through any domestic channel — and replacing a full block with a narrower, more precisely targeted consequence: persons are never cut off; only local hosting and local money are.

**6.9.1 Two statuses; what each means.** Every jurisdiction is, under this section, either **TRUE** or **UNKNOWN** — verified under §6.9.2–§6.9.3 and recorded under §6.9.8. A **TRUE** jurisdiction is fully and unconditionally within §6.2's ordinary promise: a product or service may be hosted, incorporated, operated, and paid there like anywhere else, with nothing further to prove. An **UNKNOWN** jurisdiction — whether not yet assessed, assessed and failing, or reverted under §6.9.9 — is not cut off from persons, but is cut off from infrastructure and money: §6.9.5 (No Local Presence) and §6.9.6 (Zero Local Remittance) apply to it in place of unconditional access, for as long as it remains UNKNOWN. Denying the product or service to a person because their jurisdiction is UNKNOWN, rather than serving them under §6.9.5–§6.9.6's structural conditions, is itself an ordinary §6.2 breach — the same breach it would be for any other reason. A jurisdiction's UNKNOWN status does not, by itself, say anything adverse about the jurisdiction, its government, or its people — it says only that its own law does not yet meet the one test in §6.9.2, or that this has not yet been publicly verified. Within an UNKNOWN jurisdiction, service to a natural person is additionally subject to §6.9.14's personal-use default — a condition on the *terms* of service, never a ground to withhold it. This TRUE/UNKNOWN status is Indicator I of the three this section defines; §6.9.16 and §6.9.17 state Indicators II and III, and §6.9.18 states how all three combine.

**6.9.2 The Equality Clause — a single provision is enough; only absolute unamendability is not.** A jurisdiction's status is **TRUE** the moment both of the following are satisfied and publicly verifiable:

**(a) A public, written equality clause.** Some public, written, identifiable legal or foundational text of that jurisdiction — which may be as short as a single article, section, or clause, and need not be a comprehensive, multi-chapter, formally codified constitution — states, directly and operatively, that **all human beings**, not only citizens, nationals, residents, or adherents of a particular status, are equal by birth in fundamental legal standing, without distinction as to ethnicity, religion, national or peoplehood origin, or ancestry. A preamble, political declaration, ordinary statute silent on its own permanence, judicial gloss on a vaguer general clause, or citizenship-only formula does not satisfy this subsection on its own — the clause itself must say what (a) requires, in those terms.

**(b) Absolutely unamendable — by anyone, through anything.** That specific clause cannot be repealed, suspended, derogated from, or narrowed through **any** procedure that jurisdiction's own legal system recognizes — ordinary legislation, constitutional amendment however demanding, supermajority vote, popular referendum, executive decree, or emergency or state-of-exception power, all included without exception. This is the entire test's dispositive element: if there exists **any** domestic mechanism, however difficult, symbolic, rare, or extraordinary, by which that jurisdiction's own parliament, executive, judiciary, or electorate could lawfully change or remove the clause, this subsection is not satisfied — full stop, regardless of how elaborate or minimal the clause itself is, and regardless of how unlikely that mechanism is ever to be used. A clause that could, even only in theory and even only through the single most demanding procedure that jurisdiction's own law provides, be amended or removed, does not satisfy this subsection merely because it has not yet been.

**(c) Ceremonial and honorific titles disregarded.** A hereditary, ceremonial, religious, or honorific title, rank, or style — including a title of nobility, knighthood, peerage, or comparable precedence — is not evidence against a jurisdiction's status under this section, provided it confers no enforceable civil, political, immigration, or economic right or status unavailable on identical terms to a person outside the class that holds it. This section tests equality of legal rights and status by birth; it does not test the existence of ceremony, symbol, or address.

**(d) What "equal in fundamental legal standing" tests, and what it does not.** This section tests **formal** legal equality — equal standing before the law, equal legal protection of life, body, and physical security, and equal legal personhood, regardless of birth-linked status — not the existence, scope, or generosity of any particular welfare, healthcare, or social-provision system. A jurisdiction is not disqualified from TRUE merely because it lacks an entrenched universal right to healthcare, food, housing, or similar material provision — vanishingly few legal systems entrench rights of that kind at all, and requiring it would turn this section into a different, far broader inquiry than the equal-standing test it is. It **is** disqualified, however, where the law itself values, protects, or punishes harm to a human life or body differently according to ethnicity, religion, national or peoplehood origin, ancestry, or comparable birth-linked status — for example, a lesser criminal penalty for killing or harming a person of one group than another, or a narrower legal right of self-defense, rescue, or protection for one group than another — because that is exactly the unequal fundamental legal standing (a)–(c) already test, not a separate, positive-rights inquiry this section does not undertake. Equal material provision of life-sustaining goods by a product or service — as opposed to equal legal standing under a jurisdiction's own law — is addressed directly, and independently of any jurisdiction's status, at §6.11.

Where good-faith doubt exists whether (a) or (b) is satisfied, the doubt is resolved against TRUE: this section requires certainty, not a plausible argument, and UNKNOWN is the default in any case of genuine doubt.

**6.9.3 Evidence Track — only where no single clause exists, and only on the same entrenchment logic.** A jurisdiction with no written instrument capable of satisfying §6.9.2(a) may still reach TRUE, but only by a showing, verified under §6.9.8, that: **(a)** a court of last resort in that jurisdiction has actually and finally recognized an equality-by-birth principle meeting §6.9.2(a)'s substance as legally binding and as forming a permanent part of that jurisdiction's fundamental legal order; and **(b)** that recognition is itself, under that jurisdiction's own law, beyond the reach of any procedure — legislative, judicial, executive, or popular — to reverse, narrow, or overrule, on the same absolute terms §6.9.2(b) requires. A non-binding declaration, a statute amendable like any other, a ratified but non-self-executing international instrument, a change of government policy, or a diplomatic or ministerial assurance satisfies neither element. This pathway is not a lesser or easier substitute for §6.9.2; it exists only for the case where the same substantive guarantee is genuinely, permanently entrenched without ever having been written into a single clause.

**6.9.4 Sub-national and federal application.** Where a right or status is actually exercised, granted, or withheld at a sub-national level — a state, province, region, or autonomous entity — this section is applied at that level for that specific right or status, even where the jurisdiction's national-level instrument independently satisfies §6.9.2. A jurisdiction whose national instrument satisfies §6.9.2, but one of whose constituent units retains, through any domestic procedure, the power to condition civil, political, economic, immigration, or citizenship rights on ethnicity, religion, national or peoplehood origin, or ancestry within a domain that unit genuinely controls, is UNKNOWN with respect to that unit's exercise of that domain, and TRUE with respect to everything else.

**6.9.5 No Local Presence.** For as long as a jurisdiction is UNKNOWN, no server, data center, registered office, incorporated entity, employee, contractor, or other material operational infrastructure for the product or service reaching that jurisdiction may be based, domiciled, or physically located within it. "Based" means the place from which the product or service is actually hosted, incorporated, managed, and operationally controlled — not the personal residence, nationality, or physical location of any individual team member or of the (God) Father personally: a (God) Father may live anywhere, including an UNKNOWN jurisdiction, provided the entity, hosting, and operational control of the product or service itself genuinely sit elsewhere. Where a (God) Father operates through an entity under §2.2, and is, in substance, the entire operation — a sole individual whose own base of work is that entity's infrastructure — that base itself is what this subsection reaches, and it must be relocated exactly as a server or registered office would be. Where a (God) Father instead acts directly under §2.1, with no entity at all, this subsection does not reach their own person or workplace merely because they live or work in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction — see §6.9.15(b) for why, and §6.9.14 for the terms on which they may nonetheless offer the product or service to others.

**6.9.6 Zero Local Remittance.** For as long as a jurisdiction is UNKNOWN, no revenue-share payment under §10, royalty, fee, dividend, profit distribution, or other transfer of value arising from that product or service's operation may be paid, remitted, settled, or otherwise directed to any person, account, or entity within it — except the minimum, unavoidable transaction cost a bona fide, independent third-party payment processor or financial intermediary retains solely to complete a user's own payment, which is the intermediary's ordinary cost of business, not a remittance by the operator, and does not breach this subsection. A tax, withholding, or similar sum that jurisdiction's government lawfully and unavoidably imposes directly on a transaction with a person located there, as a matter of generally applicable law rather than an arrangement the operator chose, is likewise not a breach of this subsection by itself — but the operator may not maintain a local subsidiary, revenue-sharing arrangement, licensing-back structure, "service fee," "cost reimbursement," loan, or profit-repatriation device whose purpose or effect is to route revenue derived from this License into that jurisdiction beyond what such non-discretionary local law actually requires. Ordinary wages, salary, or a consulting fee paid for labor genuinely performed by a person located in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction — market-rate compensation for work actually done, not a share of profit or a return on the product or service's own commercial performance — is not "revenue... arising from that product or service's operation" within the meaning of this subsection and is not restricted by it: this subsection reaches distributions of License-derived value, not the ordinary cost of employing or contracting with people wherever they live. Revenue earned from users in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction is not exempt from §10's ordinary revenue-share obligation on that account — it is calculated, owed, and paid exactly as it would be anywhere else; this subsection only forbids where it may be sent. §6.9.14 separately, and additionally, restricts whether a commercial, revenue-generating transaction with a natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction may be entered into at all — the two subsections apply together, not as alternatives.

**6.9.7 No workaround.** No Recipient, (God) Father, entity, or government may avoid §6.9.5 or §6.9.6 by: incorporating on paper in a TRUE jurisdiction while actual hosting, control, staff, or operations remain in fact within an UNKNOWN one; layering payments through one or more intermediary entities whose practical effect is to deliver value into an UNKNOWN jurisdiction; mislabeling a remittance to evade §6.9.6; characterizing a product or service reaching an UNKNOWN jurisdiction as "not operated" there while it is in fact accessible to, marketed to, or materially relied upon by persons in it; obtaining an Artifact through a channel described in §1.3 and operating infrastructure or routing payments there regardless; or any other structuring device whose practical effect is the same. A product or service accessible to persons in a jurisdiction is reaching that jurisdiction for the purposes of this section, whether or not the operator considers itself to be "in" it. The Dormant Sliding Fallback (§12) does not excuse a breach of §6.9.5 or §6.9.6: no AGPL, no CC BY-SA, no lesser substitute stands in for these structural conditions in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction.

**6.9.8 Public determination; no self-certification.** The Custodian shall maintain, at the Registry, a public record of every jurisdiction's status under this section — UNKNOWN or TRUE, and if TRUE, under §6.9.2 or §6.9.3 — together with the instrument, ruling, or dossier relied upon and the Custodian's stated reasons, including reasons for declining to find TRUE. A Recipient, a (God) Father, or a jurisdiction itself may submit a Jurisdictional Equality Dossier toward a determination; until a Veche exists, the Custodian publishes a reasoned provisional determination, and after a Veche exists, the Veche determines the matter under transparent procedure. A Recipient's own legal memorandum, or a government's own assurance, is evidence toward that determination — never the determination itself. In forming a determination, the Custodian or Veche may rely on independent, non-partisan comparative-constitutional sources — apex-court rulings, recognized comparative-law databases, equivalent scholarly or intergovernmental material — without being required to reconstruct each jurisdiction's law from first principles; such reliance does not relieve the Custodian or Veche of applying this section's own test rather than a source's own characterization. Compliance with §6.9.5–§6.9.6 in a given case is an ordinary question for §8's suspicion-triggered audit, and this entire record is part of the License's provenance chain under §4.3.

**6.9.9 Continuing duty; automatic reversion; transition.** A TRUE status is not a one-time determination. If a jurisdiction that reached TRUE later repeals, suspends, narrows, or derogates from the qualifying clause or recognition — or if any domestic mechanism to do so is newly created where §6.9.2(b) previously found none — its status automatically reverts to UNKNOWN from the effective date of that change, without need for further notice. A Recipient or (God) Father must monitor for a change of this kind and publish notice of it without delay; failing to do so, or continuing to operate without disclosing a known reversion, is concealment and an independent Fruits Test breach under §8, on the same footing as §4.6. On a reversion, or on an initial UNKNOWN determination for a jurisdiction where a product or service was already lawfully hosting infrastructure or remitting payments under an earlier version of this License, the operator has a transition period — as promptly as reasonably practicable, and in any case within the same period §6.3 would allow for a comparable legal-conflict withdrawal, publicly logged under §6.5's standard — to relocate infrastructure under §6.9.5 and stop local remittance under §6.9.6, without interrupting service to persons there. This is consistent with §13's Ratchet Principle that no right already granted is diminished without transition: it is operators, not end-users, who must adjust, and they are given a fair window to do it in. Continuing to host infrastructure or remit payments there under this License after that window closes is an ordinary breach of §6.9.5 or §6.9.6.

**6.9.10 Radical Symmetry in application.** This section is applied identically regardless of the Custodian's own nationality, residence, or religion (§6.6), and identically regardless of the size, power, alignment, or prominence of the jurisdiction assessed. A determination under §6.9.8 that cannot be defended as the same conclusion this section's text would compel for any other jurisdiction on materially identical facts is not a proper application of it, and is itself challengeable under §8 on the same terms as any other claimed breach of Radical Symmetry.

**6.9.11 Initial rollout.** Because §6.9.5–§6.9.6 apply to every UNKNOWN jurisdiction from the first moment this License takes effect, the Custodian shall, before or concurrently with signature, publish an initial public Jurisdictional Equality Status Table applying §6.9.2–§6.9.3 to every jurisdiction in which a Corpus-based product or service is then known to the Custodian to be hosted, operated, or paid, and shall add any other jurisdiction to that table, on the same terms, on request through the §6.9.8 dossier process. A jurisdiction not yet assessed remains UNKNOWN in the meantime, exactly as §6.9.1 provides. **As of 14 September 2026, that initial table shows zero of the 193 UN member states as TRUE — every one is UNKNOWN, none automatically, none by default, and none exempted; this is the honest starting position §6.9.2's demanding test produces on a first pass, not a defect in it, and §6.9.15 exists precisely to keep this License operable while that remains the case.**

**6.9.12 Non-severable; no fallback.** This section exists to give §6.2 an administrable, jurisdiction-blind operative standard without ever letting a jurisdiction's own legal defect fall on the persons who live there, and stands on the same non-severable, no-fallback footing as §6.2–§6.5 under §6.7: if its operation is held ineffective in any forum, the remainder is interpreted to maximize alignment with it — never by silently dropping §6.9.5, §6.9.6, §6.9.14, or §6.9.15 while keeping the rest of this License intact — and only if that is impossible does the remainder of this License become void in that jurisdiction, on the same terms §6.7 already provides.

**6.9.13 Left for Counsel.** This section states a test and a structural consequence, not a jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction legal conclusion. Whether any particular jurisdiction in fact satisfies §6.9.2 or §6.9.3 as of a given date is a question of that jurisdiction's own law, to be verified under §6.9.8 and, where a Recipient's own exposure turns on it, confirmed with qualified local counsel; nothing in this section or the companion materials constitutes a legal conclusion about any specific jurisdiction's present constitutional status. Open questions the Author has identified but not resolved include: the practical means of verifying, on audit, where infrastructure is genuinely "based" for purposes of §6.9.5 in a world of distributed and cloud-hosted systems; whether capital or investment originating from within an UNKNOWN jurisdiction raises a concern distinct from the outbound remittance §6.9.6 addresses; the treatment of directly-effective supranational or regional human-rights instruments a jurisdiction has not itself designated as meeting §6.9.2(a); the treatment of non-self-governing, occupied, or disputed territories where more than one legal order claims to govern the same population; the evidentiary weight to give a jurisdiction's own highest court where that court's authority to bind the legislature is itself contested under that jurisdiction's law; the test for where a natural person is "located," for purposes of §6.9.14, where declared residence, billing address, network-derived geolocation, and actual physical presence diverge; and whether an indirect consumption tax a payment processor collects and remits automatically, without the operator's own discretion, should be treated under §6.9.14(c) the way §6.9.6 already treats an unavoidable, non-discretionary local tax, or whether §6.9.14's "no price where any tax would attach" rule is stricter by design and admits no such carve-out. These remain, as with the comparable open questions already flagged elsewhere in this License (§0.2), matters for the forthcoming SVE Interpretive Guidance and for counsel in the jurisdiction concerned, not resolved by silence or by omission here.

**6.9.14 Commercial-Use Ceiling for Natural Persons in UNKNOWN Jurisdictions — Personal Use Free; Commercial Use Only at Zero Local Tax.** This is the same structural distinction §6.9.5–§6.9.6 already draw — a condition tied to a jurisdiction's own demonstrated legal status, identical for every jurisdiction on Earth under the identical test, never to any person's nationality, ethnicity, or identity — extended from infrastructure and remittance to the terms of commercial engagement itself. Within a jurisdiction that is UNKNOWN under this section, a Corpus-based product or service remains fully available to every natural person there under §6.2 and §6.9.1, on the following terms, in addition to §6.9.5 and §6.9.6:

**(a) Personal-use default.** A natural person located in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction may use the product or service, free of charge, for their own personal, non-commercial, educational, or individual-research purposes, without restriction. This includes ordinary individual use, self-directed learning, and research conducted and published in their own name; it does not include operating the product or service as, through, or on behalf of a commercial enterprise, a government body, or any other entity, or reselling, sublicensing, or integrating it into a good or service offered to others for consideration.

**(b) Bona fide non-commercial institutions.** A non-profit educational institution, library, museum, research institute, or humanitarian organization physically located in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction is treated the same as a natural person under subsection (a) for its own genuinely free, non-revenue-generating public-interest use — it may not act as a paid reseller, commercial integrator, or revenue-generating intermediary, but its institutional form alone is never a reason to withhold from it what a natural person already receives free.

**(c) Commercial use permitted only at zero local tax.** A natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction may still be served commercially — charged a price, subscription, or fee — but only for a specific transaction that generates no tax, levy, duty, withholding, or other fiscal payment, direct or indirect, to that jurisdiction's government or any sub-national authority within it. Where that jurisdiction's generally applicable law would impose such a payment on the transaction (for example, a sales tax or value-added tax collected on a paid subscription), the commercial grant is unavailable for that transaction in that jurisdiction; the operator's only lawful options are to furnish it free of charge under subsection (a), or to withhold that specific commercial feature from persons there under §6.3's ordinary selective-withdrawal logic, applied uniformly to everyone in that jurisdiction rather than to any individual. No price is charged where charging one would create a local tax base — an UNKNOWN jurisdiction's treasury receives nothing to tax, because nothing is sold.

**(d) TRUE jurisdictions unaffected — with a narrower fallback available.** This subsection does not apply in a TRUE jurisdiction: ordinary commercial terms under §6.2 and §10 apply there exactly as everywhere else, subject only to that jurisdiction's own generally applicable law. Where that jurisdiction's own law specifically bars a particular commercial feature the operator would otherwise offer, the operator may, instead of withdrawing the product or service entirely under §6.3, fall back to furnishing it free of charge under subsection (a) to everyone in that jurisdiction alike — a narrower, more protective option §6.3 does not itself require, but does not forbid either, since it serves strictly more people than a full withdrawal would.

**(e) Revenue-share unaffected elsewhere.** Nothing in this subsection reduces §10's ordinary revenue-share obligation on any commercial transaction actually entered into, in an UNKNOWN or a TRUE jurisdiction alike; it only narrows where a commercial transaction with a natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction may lawfully occur in the first place. Where subsection (a) or (c) requires a transaction to be free, no revenue arises from it to be owed.

**(f) No workaround.** §6.9.7's no-workaround rule applies to this subsection in full: registering, or permitting registration, as an individual to mask what is in substance an entity's or a government's use; routing payment through cryptocurrency, a nominal "donation" or "gift," an intermediary account, or any other device to obscure that a transaction would otherwise create a local taxable nexus; or structuring a nominally "personal" account that is in fact used to serve a commercial or governmental end, is a workaround under §6.9.7 and an independent breach.

**(g) Transition.** An operator already lawfully charging natural persons in a jurisdiction that is or becomes UNKNOWN, under an earlier version of this License or before this subsection's effective date, receives the same transition window §6.9.9 already provides before this subsection applies to that arrangement — consistent with §13's Ratchet Principle that operators, never end-users, absorb the adjustment, and that no one loses service they already had; the transition converts an existing paid arrangement to the free terms of subsection (a), it never simply cuts it off.

**6.9.15 No entity operation while zero jurisdictions are TRUE — natural persons may still act directly, free or at zero local tax.**

**(a) Entity operation suspended — no compromise.** For as long as zero jurisdictions are TRUE, §2.2's pathway — a legal entity operating a Corpus-based product or service through a (God) Father — is suspended in its entirety: no legal entity of any kind (corporation, LLC, partnership, foundation, government body, trust, DAO treasury, or similar) may build, operate, host, fund, or hold itself out as offering a Corpus-based product or service under this License, anywhere on Earth, under any structure, for any reason, until at least one jurisdiction is determined TRUE under §6.9.8. There is no bootstrap exception to this, no "best available" jurisdiction it may shelter in, and no disclosed workaround that cures it: an entity that operates a Corpus-based product or service while zero jurisdictions are TRUE is in ordinary, uncured breach of §2.2 and §6.9.5 alike, wherever on Earth it is based. This subsection does not reach a governance body that only receives a revenue-share payment without itself operating a product or service — per §2.5, the SVE Foundation, a community treasury, or a payment processor may still receive funds under §10 without being an operator, exactly as before. For the avoidance of doubt, this reaches SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode (§11) exactly as it reaches any other entity: a Founder Mode venture is a legal entity operating a Corpus-based product or service, and it may not do so while zero jurisdictions are TRUE, on the same terms as any other entity, no exception made for its size or founder-stage status.

**(b) Natural persons may still act directly — this was never blocked.** §6.9.15(a) reaches only the entity pathway of §2.2. It does not touch, restrict, or suspend a natural person's own right under §2.1 and §3 to build, run, modify, and offer as a Network Service any Corpus Artifact directly, in their own name, with full and unlimited personal liability and no entity standing between them and this License. A (God) Father acting this way needs no relocation, no TRUE jurisdiction to be "based" in, and no entity to hold rights on their behalf — they are this License's original, intended kind of Recipient, exactly as §2.1 already provides, and a human being living and working somewhere on Earth was never "infrastructure" for §6.9.5 to reach merely by existing there. §6.9.5's own prior text — "a sole individual whose own base of work is the infrastructure... must be relocated exactly as a server or registered office would be" — is corrected by this subsection to that extent: it no longer applies to a natural person acting directly under §2.1, only to an entity's operational base under §2.2, which §6.9.15(a) already reaches by a harder rule than relocation.

**(c) What a directly-acting natural person may and may not do.** A (God) Father operating directly under §2.1, without an entity, may use the product or service for themselves free of charge without restriction (§6.9.14(a)), and may build, run, and offer it to others — including commercially — subject to exactly the same zero-local-tax ceiling §6.9.14(c) already applies to any commercial transaction with a natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction: where a transaction under this License would generate a tax, levy, duty, or other fiscal payment to any UNKNOWN jurisdiction's government — whether because the (God) Father, the other party, or both are located in one — that transaction must instead be furnished free; where it would not, it may be charged for, and ordinary §10 revenue-share is owed on it exactly as on any other commercial transaction. *"Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar's, and to God the things that are God's"* (Matthew 22:21): nothing in this section touches a (God) Father's own, ordinary personal tax obligations to their own country of residence on income they actually and lawfully receive — that duty is theirs to meet like anyone else's, and this License neither creates nor excuses it (§6.9.6 already says the same for wages). What this subsection and §6.9.14(c) forbid is narrower and different in kind: pricing or routing a *transaction under this License* so as to hand fiscal revenue to an UNKNOWN jurisdiction's treasury *on the strength of this License's own commercial activity* — never a person's private duty to pay ordinary tax on their own personal earnings, which this License does not reach at all (§4.7).

**(d) No workaround.** §6.9.7 applies in full: an entity may not disguise itself as a "sole natural person" operation while an incorporated structure, investor cap table, limited-liability shield, or comparable arrangement actually stands behind it in substance; a (God) Father may not accept indemnification, reimbursement, or an informal corporate arrangement that quietly restores what §2.4(c) already forbids explicitly; and structuring what is, in substance, an entity's commercial operation as a chain of individually-registered "personal" accounts is a workaround under §6.9.7, independently auditable under §8. Every other duty of this License — the Fruits Test (§8), Research Integrity and the Truth-Bearer track (§9), disclosure and Anti-Enclosure (§4), the Wholeness Clause (§5) — remains fully and identically in force for a directly-acting natural person under this subsection; nothing here relaxes any of it.

**(e) Self-terminating.** The moment any jurisdiction is determined TRUE under §6.9.8, §6.9.15(a)'s suspension of §2.2 lifts for that operator's future entity formation and operations, which may then proceed in a TRUE jurisdiction on ordinary §6.9.5–§6.9.6 terms; §6.9.9's transition window applies to any (God) Father who was operating directly under §6.9.15(b)–(c) and now wishes to convert to an entity structure in a newly-TRUE jurisdiction, exactly as it would for any other operator adjusting to a status change.

**6.9.16 Indicator II — Institutional Access; the Parent–Child Reciprocity Program.** §6.9.1–§6.9.15 above state Indicator I: whether a jurisdiction is TRUE or UNKNOWN for entity operation (§6.9.5) and revenue remittance (§6.9.6). This subsection states a second, wholly independent indicator, tested and recorded separately for every jurisdiction on Earth: whether a legal entity, government body, or other institution located within that jurisdiction — as distinct from a natural person already served under §6.9.14 — may be charged for a Corpus-based product or service there. A jurisdiction's status under this Indicator has no bearing on its status under Indicator I, and Indicator I has no bearing on this one: either can be TRUE while the other is UNKNOWN, in any combination, and each is determined, recorded, and reversed entirely on its own terms.

**(a) Default: no grant subsists — the burden rests on the jurisdiction and the institution alike.** Unless and until both **(i)** this Indicator is TRUE for the institution's own jurisdiction under (b) below, and **(ii)** the institution is itself represented by a named natural person, personally and individually accountable for its compliance and its fruits, on the same terms §2.2–§2.4 already require of an institutional operator — standing behind the institution's use of this License without thereby exercising rights under §3 or becoming a Recipient — no grant of any kind subsists under this License for that institution to receive a Corpus-based product or service, commercially or otherwise. This is not a denial under §6.2 any more than §6.9.15(a)'s identical, already-established suspension of all entity operation is one: §6.2's promise to "every person and entity" is given its operative, verifiable content by this Indicator exactly as §6.9.0 already provides for §6.9.15, and no institution may claim an unconditioned grant merely because it has not yet been verified. A natural person's own access stands on the opposite default in every respect — granted from the moment this License attaches, revocable only by an audit-proven bad-fruits finding, never by a mere absence of proof — see §6.9.19. A bona fide non-profit institution already covered by §6.9.14(b) is unaffected by this subsection and keeps that subsection's own, separate, unconditional free-access terms; this subsection reaches a commercial enterprise, a government body, or another institution outside §6.9.14(b)'s narrower scope.

**(b) Reaching TRUE: the Parent role.** A jurisdiction reaches TRUE under this Indicator by its own competent public authority formally and publicly committing, verified under §6.9.8's non-self-certifying process on the same terms as Indicator I, to both of the following for a six-plus-one-year term (the "Cycle"): **(i)** directing 10% of whatever revenue is actually collected under §10 from commercial transactions with institutions located in that jurisdiction to a single other jurisdiction (the "Child") — this amount is naturally zero in any period where no such revenue arises, and the commitment is not otherwise reduced or excused on that account; and **(ii)** devoting real, substantial effort — training, mentorship, technical assistance, and genuine knowledge- and skill-transfer toward whatever the Child jurisdiction's own people and institutions actually seek to learn — to that same Child, unconditionally on whether (i) ever generates a material amount, and disclosed and audited under (f).

**(c) Selecting the Child.** The Child is selected from a public pool of jurisdictions that have themselves, through their own competent public authority, separately and voluntarily consented to be eligible as a Child, by the same honest, unpredictable, unbribable lottery method §6.9.8 and §6.11(d) already require for comparable determinations — never by the Parent's own choice, and never imposed on a jurisdiction that has not itself consented to be considered.

**(d) The Cycle.** Years 1–4: active teaching and capacity-building at the Parent's own initiative, alongside the 10% share on qualifying revenue. Year 5: the Parent shifts to observation and correction, continuing to advise and audit progress, the 10% share continuing. Year 6: observation and consultation only, on request; the 10% share ends for that year, and everything the Child's institutions earn in Year 6 stays within the Child's own jurisdiction. Year 7: a rest year, with no obligation on either side. At the close of Year 7, provided the Parent's status has not reverted under (g), a new Child is drawn under (c) for a new Cycle.

**(e) The mutual case.** Where two jurisdictions are each independently drawn as the other's Child in the same round, each simply also becomes the other's Parent under this subsection, at the same time — teaching what the other lacks and receiving what it itself lacks in turn. This subsection does not prevent that outcome, and does not need to: two peoples who happen to need each other's help in different rooms are not a defect in this Program.

**(f) Disclosure and audit.** A Parent jurisdiction's compliance with (b)(ii) must be publicly disclosed at least annually, in concrete enough detail — what was taught, to whom, and what changed — for §8's Fruits Test to audit it on suspicion, on the same footing as §9.2's Field-Notes Duty. Collecting the 10% share under (b)(i) while providing only nominal, pro forma, or fabricated assistance under (b)(ii) is concealment, and an independent Fruits Test breach under §8, exactly as §4.6 and §6.9.9 already treat comparable concealment elsewhere in this section.

**(g) Automatic reversion.** If a Parent fails to remit the 10% share when due, or is shown on audit under (f) to have provided only nominal or fabricated assistance, its status under this Indicator automatically reverts to UNKNOWN from that failure's effective date, on the same automatic-reversion, operator-transition-window terms §6.9.9 already provides for Indicator I; the Cycle in progress ends, and this subsection does not permit that jurisdiction to re-enter as a Parent before a full further Cycle's worth of time has passed.

**(h) Payment channel.** The 10% share is collected and remitted through the same revenue-share collection and reporting mechanism §10 and Meta-License v4.0 Appendix B already use, and, consistent with §2.5, may pass through the SVE Foundation or a comparable treasury as an intermediary without that body becoming a Recipient; it is drawn from revenue already collected under §10, never an additional charge layered on top of it.

**(i) Non-severable; no fallback; independent of Indicator I.** This subsection stands on the same non-severable, no-fallback footing as §6.9.5–§6.9.6 and §6.9.14, under §6.9.12: no AGPL, no CC BY-SA, and no lesser rung of §12 stands in for it. A jurisdiction's participation as Parent or Child under this Program never substitutes for, offsets, or is offset by its own status under Indicator I — each remains its own, independent floor.

**6.9.17 Indicator III — the Gate: a substantive floor beneath Indicators I and II.** §6.9.2(d) already limits Indicator I to formal legal equality — the text of a jurisdiction's law — and expressly leaves positive, material rights outside its test. This subsection adds a different, narrower floor beneath that text: not what the law promises, but whether, in a jurisdiction's ordinary civic life — its schools, courts, media, public administration, and public employment — a documented, sustained pattern actually suppresses a group's ethnicity, national or peoplehood origin, ancestry, religion, or language, regardless of what the jurisdiction's own constitutional text says. This subsection names no country, people, or conflict, anywhere in its own text, consistent with §6.9.0's neutrality commitment; every application of it is a case-by-case public determination under §6.9.8, on documented fact, never on this text's own characterization of any real-world situation.

**(a) Two states; the default is unaffected.** Every jurisdiction starts, and remains, PASSING under this subsection unless and until shown otherwise under (b) — an unassessed or genuinely disputed jurisdiction is PASSING, exactly as an unassessed jurisdiction is UNKNOWN, and not TRUE, under Indicator I; a PASSING determination carries no consequence at all for Indicators I or II, which stand or fall entirely on their own terms. Only a jurisdiction affirmatively shown FAILING under (b) is affected, and only in the way (d) states.

**(b) What FAILING requires.** A jurisdiction is FAILING under this subsection only where a documented, sustained pattern — not an isolated incident, and not a merely alleged or genuinely disputed one — of suppressing a group's ethnicity, national or peoplehood origin, ancestry, religion, or language in ordinary civic life is shown by at least one of: **(i)** a finding of a United Nations human-rights treaty body or comparable intergovernmental human-rights mechanism with a mandate reaching that jurisdiction; **(ii)** a judgment of an international court or tribunal with jurisdiction over the matter; **(iii)** a final ruling of that jurisdiction's own court of last resort acknowledging the pattern; or **(iv)** the testimony of at least two independent, identifiable, firsthand witnesses, assessed under (b-1) below. A single incident — even one several witnesses describe together — an unproven allegation, an advocacy organization's own unadjudicated report standing alone, or a live, genuinely contested factual dispute does not satisfy this subsection. Where good-faith doubt exists whether this subsection's evidentiary standard is met, the doubt is resolved against FAILING, on the same certainty-first logic §6.9.2's closing paragraph already applies to Indicator I.

**(b-1) Witness testimony: what makes it sufficient, and its protections.** People who actually live the pattern this subsection addresses are themselves a source — often the only source, where the institutions (i)–(iii) rely on will not or cannot act against their own government. Testimony under (b)(iv) is sufficient where: it comes from real, identifiable individuals, traceable to the Custodian or, once it exists, the Veche, on the same terms §2.4 already requires for a (God) Father's pseudonym, even where a witness's name is withheld from the public record; there are at least two such witnesses — a third or more strengthens the showing but is not itself required; each describes the pattern itself, from their own firsthand experience or direct observation, not a single occurrence and not something merely heard about; and the witnesses are independent of each other and of whoever submits the dossier — not coordinated, not compensated for testifying, and not drawn from a single organization or campaign dressed up as several separate voices. A witness's safety is protected exactly as §9.5 already protects a source: their identity may be withheld from the public record while remaining verified, privately, by the Custodian or Veche. Knowingly fabricated, coached, or coordinated-to-appear-independent testimony is a Fruits Test breach under §8, on the same footing as §9.3's bar on fabricated research results, and taints the entire dossier it was submitted in — this is in addition to, not instead of, §6.9.17(e)'s Reciprocal-Audit-Priority safeguard, which applies to whoever brings the claim regardless of which evidentiary category it rests on.

**(c) Automatic reversion.** If the pattern found under (b) is credibly shown to have ended or been remedied — by a later finding, ruling, or judgment from the same category of source, or by fresh testimony meeting (b-1)'s own terms — the jurisdiction's status reverts to PASSING from that finding's effective date, on the same terms §6.9.9 already provides for Indicator I; this subsection does not hold a past failure against a jurisdiction once the underlying pattern is genuinely gone.

**(d) Effect: it zeroes, it does not itself decide.** For as long as a jurisdiction is FAILING under this subsection, its status under Indicator I (§6.9.1–§6.9.15) and Indicator II (§6.9.16) is treated as UNKNOWN for every purpose under this License, regardless of what either would otherwise show on its own terms — a jurisdiction cannot be treated as TRUE under either Indicator while FAILING here. A PASSING or unassessed jurisdiction's Indicator I and Indicator II statuses are entirely unaffected by this subsection and are decided solely under §6.9.1–§6.9.15 and §6.9.16 respectively. This subsection never itself supplies a TRUE finding for either Indicator; it only ever withholds one.

**(e) Reciprocal-Audit-Priority applies with particular force.** Because a FAILING determination under this subsection carries real consequences and touches inherently contested questions, §8.3's rule — that whoever initiates a suspicion-based claim submits to the same audit first or at the same time, never after — applies to any claim that a jurisdiction is FAILING under this subsection exactly as it applies to any other breach allegation, with no relaxation; a party that will not submit to that same scrutiny has no standing to trigger this subsection's consequence.

**(f) Non-severable; no fallback.** This subsection stands on the same non-severable, no-fallback footing as §6.9.5–§6.9.6, §6.9.14, and §6.9.16, under §6.9.12.

**6.9.18 How the three Indicators combine.** In summary: Indicator I (§6.9.1–§6.9.15, TRUE/UNKNOWN) governs entity operation and revenue remittance. Indicator II (§6.9.16, TRUE/UNKNOWN) governs whether a jurisdiction's own institutions may be paying customers. Indicator III (§6.9.17, PASSING/FAILING, "the Gate") governs neither directly; it only ever withholds — a FAILING Gate treats Indicator I and Indicator II alike as UNKNOWN, however either would otherwise read, while a PASSING or unassessed Gate leaves both entirely to their own, independent tests. No combination of these three ever reduces what a natural person already receives free under §6.2 and §6.9.14(a): those floors do not depend on any of the three Indicators, and nothing in this subsection or §6.9.16–§6.9.17 touches them.

**6.9.19 The Asymmetric Default — natural persons served unless proven bad fruit; entities and institutions never presumed.** This section's three Indicators operate against a single, deliberately asymmetric background rule, restating explicitly what §6.2, §6.4, and §8.4 (Asymmetric Rigor) already establish as this License's general design. A natural person's access under §6.2 and §6.9.14 is granted by default — it requires no indicator, no dossier, no showing of anything, and is TRUE the moment this License attaches (§1.2) — and it remains in force unless and until §8's Fruits Test, following a suspicion-triggered audit conducted under §8.3's reciprocal-priority sequencing, establishes that this specific person's own conduct produced bad fruit; §6.4 already governs exactly this consequence, and this subsection adds nothing to it beyond naming, once, the default it has always implied. A legal entity, government body, or other institution receives the opposite default: no grant of any kind subsists for it under this License — as an operator (§6.9.15(a)) or as a customer (§6.9.16(a)) — until the burden resting on both its own jurisdiction and on the institution itself has been affirmatively discharged, under the specific terms §6.9.15 and §6.9.16 each state; absence of proof is not evidence of good fruit for an entity the way it already is for a person. This is not a lesser protection for institutions than for persons, and is not meant to be one: it is the same conviction the Natural-Person Rule (§2) has held since v5.5 — this License trusts a human being, accountable in their own name and body, by default, and trusts a corporate or sovereign structure not at all until it has earned that trust in the open, the same way anyone else does. Non-severable on the same footing as §6.9.12.

**6.10 The Golden Rule — reversibility as the test for good fruit.** *"So whatever you wish that others would do to you, do also to them, for this is the Law and the Prophets."* — Matthew 7:12. Wherever this License, the Corpus, or a product or service built on it calls for a judgment the text does not spell out in full — how to rank a queue, how to phrase a disclosure, how to weigh a hard case under the Fruits Test (§8.1), how to design an allocation, a penalty, or an audit — the operative test is reversibility: would the person making the call accept the identical rule, applied to them, if their position and the affected person's were exactly exchanged? A rule, allocation, or practice its own author would not accept having imposed on themselves is bad fruit under §8.1, regardless of how it is labeled, justified, or dressed up as policy. This is not a new obligation standing beside Radical Symmetry (§6.2, §6.6) and Reciprocal-Audit-Priority (§8.3) — it is the one principle those two already express, each in their own narrower domain, stated once here, generally, so it reaches every case neither of them individually names — including §6.11 immediately below. It binds identically regardless of who applies it, the Custodian included (§6.6): no one is exempt from a rule they would not accept facing themselves.

**6.11 Scarce Resource Allocation — equal worth of life; need, then an honest lot.** Where a product or service built on a Corpus Artifact determines, ranks, recommends, or materially influences who receives a scarce resource on which a person's life, physical safety, or essential subsistence genuinely depends — emergency medical treatment, a vaccine or medicine in short supply, rescue, evacuation, shelter, or food or water in a crisis, and similarly urgent goods — the following applies, in addition to §6.1's absolute bars and §8's Fruits Test generally. This subsection governs decisions about survival, safety, and essential subsistence specifically; it does not extend this machinery to ordinary commercial queueing or the allocation of non-essential goods, which §10 and ordinary market terms continue to govern.

**(a) Equal, unconditional worth of every life.** Every human life carries identical worth, regardless of birthplace, nationality, citizenship, ethnicity, religion, wealth, status, occupation, prior conduct, or perceived usefulness to others. No product or service under this License may rank, score, or weight a person's claim to a life-or-safety-critical resource by any such measure. A "social credit," "social utility," productivity, or comparable status-based scoring mechanism applied to who lives, who is protected, or who is rescued sits alongside §6.1(b)'s bar on mass covert surveillance and repression as an absolute bar in its own right, void *ab initio*, carrying §6.8's consequence on breach.

**(b) No ancestral guilt or merit.** A person's claim under this section cannot be reduced or enhanced by anything about their parents, ancestry, or lineage, or by their own wealth or status — everyone begins, for purposes of this section, on the same footing, exactly as §6.9.2(c) already disregards ceremonial and honorific titles for the equality-by-birth test.

**(c) Presence, not birthplace, governs urgent rescue.** A person present in a place and in genuine need of urgent, life-or-safety-critical help has the same claim to it as a person born or ordinarily resident there; this section draws no distinction by birthplace, immigration status, or how the person came to be present, consistent with §6.2's Universal Access.

**(d) Need first, then an honest, unpredictable, unbribable lot.** Where the resource cannot meet the objective, genuine, and urgent need of everyone who has it, priority goes first to whoever needs it most urgently to survive or avoid serious, irreversible harm — an objective clinical, factual, or comparably verifiable determination, never a status judgment. Where need is, on the best available honest assessment, materially equal among more people than the resource can reach, the allocation among them is decided by an impartial, transparent, unpredictable, and unbribable random method — a genuine lottery or equivalent — never by status, wealth, connections, citizenship, ethnicity, religion, fame, or claimed future usefulness. *"The lot is cast into the lap, but its every decision is from the LORD"* (Proverbs 16:33) — the Corpus's own drafting tradition already trusts an honest lot as the answer no human favoritism can corrupt (cf. Acts 1:26). Reasonable, good-faith people can and do disagree on exactly how much weight, if any, a narrow clinical or resource-efficiency factor — for example, a materially higher chance of the treatment succeeding for one candidate than another — should carry before a lot is drawn among the rest; this section does not resolve that debate by rigid formula, and treats it as a matter for the SVE Interpretive Guidance and, where relevant, qualified bioethics and medical input (§6.9.13's "Left for Counsel" logic applies equally here). What it forecloses absolutely, without debate, is allocating on status, wealth, or social utility rather than genuine need or an honest lot.

**(e) Disclosed and auditable.** The criteria and method actually used for an allocation under this section — including whether and how a lot was drawn — must be disclosed in advance where practicable, and are always subject to §8's Fruits Test audit and, where research is involved, §9's Field-Notes Duty; concealing or misrepresenting the method actually used is an independent Fruits Test breach.

### §7 — Patent & Enclosure Shield
The Registry is a public, timestamped disclosure and prior art against private patenting of what it describes. Patent-holders among Recipients license compliant users to practice their patents for Corpus purposes; initiating patent litigation, or enclosing a Derivative, terminates that actor's rights (curable within 30 days of notice; not curable on repeat). Where EU or equivalent law grants a *sui generis* database right or other ancillary right in the Registry or a dataset Artifact, the Custodian exercises it under these same terms — an added layer, never a separate closed one.

### §8 — Fruits Test & Reciprocal Audit Priority ("Glass House Rule")
**8.1** §0 of Meta-License v4.0 (Fruits Test) remains supreme, unweakened — the one standard everything else in this License exists to serve.

**8.2 End-User Fruits Duty.** The Fruits Test does not stop at the operator. Anyone who *uses* a product or service built on a Corpus Artifact — not only the Recipient who built it — must apply that use toward good fruits: benefit, not harm, to persons, non-human beings, and ecosystems. Use toward bad fruits is grounds for a suspicion-triggered audit under §8.3, reaching the end-user directly, not only whoever served them.

**8.3 Reciprocal priority.** Whoever initiates a suspicion-based audit or breach report — against a Recipient, a (God) Father, or an end-user — must submit to the same audit, on the same subject, **first or at the same time — never after** (elevating and sharpening Appendix G §3A). A refusal voids the audit request; the initiator bears its cost; a repeated bad-faith demand triggers the Anti-Judas Protocol (Appendix F §6, 3× penalty).

**8.4 Asymmetric Rigor ("Narrow Gate").** This License is deliberately asymmetric. For a Recipient with clean hands and good fruits, its burdens amount to almost nothing: no permission needed, no fee for research or truth-bearing use, and a suspicion-audit a compliant party can simply answer. For a Recipient shown to have acted in bad faith — willful concealment, willful fabrication, selective compliance, or exploitation — the same mechanisms apply at full and uncompromising strength: no cure period where §6.8 already withholds one, the full weight of the One-Bit Rule and the Anti-Judas Protocol's 3× penalty, and no discount for good conduct elsewhere — prior compliance does not offset a proven present breach. A Recipient who refuses to cooperate with a properly-initiated audit under §8.3, or who obstructs, delays, or conceals records from one, is treated as having supplied the adverse evidence itself. None of this is vindictive: restoration remains open through Appendix F's Betrayal & Restoration Protocol on the same terms it always has — full transparency, no minimization — this section only makes explicit that the path is narrow, not that it is closed (cf. Matthew 7:13–14).

### §9 — Research, Investigation & Truth-Bearer Use
**9.1 Research is already free — here it is explicit.** Academic, scientific, and independent research use of any Corpus Artifact — including failed, partial, negative, or null-result experiments — needs no separate permission and no separate fee beyond §10's ordinary terms: it is already covered by the Grant (§3) and Anti-Enclosure (§4) like any other use. This section adds what research specifically needs: a duty to publish what was actually found (§9.2), and a rule against faking it (§9.3).

**9.2 Field-Notes Duty.** A Recipient who conducts research using a Corpus Artifact — funded or unfunded, academic, independent, or corporate R&D — must make available a field-notes record of that research: methodology, and both positive and negative/null results of material experiments performed with or on the Artifact. This extends §4.2's disclosure duty to the research process itself: publicizing a positive result while burying a negative one is enclosure by omission, and as much a §4 breach as hiding source code. Publication may be reasonably delayed — for safety review, peer review, or a fixed embargo disclosed in advance — but indefinite or permanent suppression of an inconvenient result is not a delay; it is a breach.

**9.3 Research Integrity.** Deliberate, willful fabrication of results, material misrepresentation of what an Artifact was found to do, or knowingly withholding what is needed to reproduce a claimed result is a Fruits Test breach, auditable on suspicion under §8.3 exactly like any other bad fruit. Honest error, a good-faith failed replication, or a negative result honestly reported are not breaches — they are precisely the field notes §9.2 exists to capture. Intent is what separates science that didn't work from science that lied.

**9.4 Truth-Bearer Track.** Anyone using a Corpus Artifact to investigate, document, verify, or expose matters of genuine public interest — journalists, whistleblowers, human-rights investigators, and similar accountability work — may do so at no cost and outside §10's revenue-share, on the same footing as non-commercial research, even where the resulting work is itself monetized (e.g., published journalism carrying advertising): the exposure and accountability *is* the fruit this License asks for. This track carries the same duties as §9.2–§9.3: methodology and substantiated findings must eventually be made available, and deliberate fabrication is a breach exactly as in §9.3.

**9.5 Source protection is not enclosure.** §9.2's and §9.4's disclosure duties never require identifying a confidential source, informant, or vulnerable subject whose safety depends on protection — disclosing methodology and substantiated findings while protecting a source's identity satisfies both duties in full. Protecting the vulnerable is itself a good fruit under §8.1, not a shortfall against it.

**9.6 Not a license to defame.** §9.4 covers good-faith investigation, not a label for harassment, exposure of private individuals absent genuine public interest, or knowingly false claims dressed as "investigation" — those remain barred by §6.1(c) and gain no cover from this section.

### §10 — Commercial Use & Revenue-Share
Commercial use of any Corpus Artifact is permitted without prior authorization, subject to §§4–9 and the revenue-share tiers of Meta-License v4.0 Appendix B. **v5.0 §3's residual CC BY-NC-SA (Non-Commercial) fallback is withdrawn** and replaced by §§4–6 above — see §0 for why this strengthens rather than weakens the framework. Revenue actually earned from users in a jurisdiction UNKNOWN under §6.9 is owed and calculated exactly like revenue from anywhere else; §6.9.6 only restricts where it may be paid, never whether it is owed. §6.9.14 separately restricts whether a commercial, revenue-generating transaction with a natural person in an UNKNOWN jurisdiction may be entered into at all — where it requires the transaction to be furnished free of charge, no revenue arises from it in the first place, and nothing is owed on a transaction this License never permitted to carry a price. §6.9.16 similarly restricts whether an institution may be a paying customer at all, in any jurisdiction, TRUE or UNKNOWN under Indicator I, until that jurisdiction separately reaches TRUE under Indicator II; the 10% share §6.9.16(b)(i) directs to a Child jurisdiction is drawn from revenue already collected under this section, never an additional charge layered on top of it.

### §11 — SVE-Unicorns Founder Mode (Cross-Reference)
For founder-stage ventures under the size thresholds of Founder Mode (≤$100M revenue, ≤1,000 staff, ≤$500M cap), the **SVE-Unicorns Patch v1.0** ("Founder Mode," signed 26.06.2026) still stands **unchanged** — this version does not reissue it, and needs no (God) Father mechanism grafted on: the founder is already, by the Patch's own design, the single named, personally-bound individual §2 now requires framework-wide — "the Custodian binds himself first" already assumed exactly this. In plain terms: a qualifying founder gets total operational freedom and may *freeze* — defer publication of — their methods until Year 44, without that freeze counting as enclosure, provided the 6 Commandments hold (audited on suspicion, per §8 above) and the work is hash-registered as SVE-bound from day one. To remove any doubt this version could create: a frozen-but-registered Artifact is **not** in breach of §4's disclosure duty or §5's Wholeness Clause — freezing defers *when* you must disclose, it does not exempt you from *that* you must eventually disclose, may never enclose, and may never sell the company. Cross the size thresholds, and Founder Mode merges into the standard 44-Year Corporate Path (Appendix B §§10–22), where the (God) Father role is naturally the CEO or equivalent officer of record. **This section is subject to §6.9.15 without exception.** A Founder Mode venture is ordinarily a legal entity, and §6.9.15(a) suspends every legal entity's right to operate a Corpus-based product or service — Founder Mode ventures included, size thresholds and founder-stage status notwithstanding — for as long as zero jurisdictions are TRUE; Radical Symmetry (§6.6) forbids carving the Custodian's own preferred commercial track out of a rule everyone else is held to. A founder who wants to build now, before any jurisdiction is TRUE, does so as a natural person directly under §2.1 and §6.9.15(b)–(c) — free, or commercial at zero local tax — and may incorporate into Founder Mode the moment a jurisdiction reaches TRUE, carrying that work's registration date and freeze forward unaffected. §4.9's Human Quarantine is this same freeze principle's individual-scale analog: available to any natural person, not only a founder-stage venture, uncapped at Year 44, and ended only by the (God) Father's own death rather than by size thresholds.

### §12 — Resilience: Dormant Sliding Fallback
Where a §3 grant, or a §4, §5, or §7 condition, is held unenforceable for a given Recipient or jurisdiction, it is replaced — for that case only — by the strongest enforceable equivalent: **L1** AGPL-3.0 (software) / CC BY-SA 4.0 (non-software); **L2** Apache-2.0 (retaining §7's patent-license and anti-aggression terms) / CC BY 4.0; **L3** attribution + the §7 covenant + continued availability. These are real, independent grants that stay dormant until the primary SVE grant actually fails for that case — never chosen, never stacked on top of a working primary grant. Because §10 removes the NC restriction, L1 no longer conflicts with the primary grant the way v5.0's cascade did — this is what fixes it. **This Ladder never reaches §6 (Ethical-Use Floor & Universal Access, including §6.9's Constitutional Equality Assurance) or §8 (Fruits Test) at any rung** — see §6.7 and §6.9.12. Nor does it ever excuse §6.9.5's No Local Presence, §6.9.6's Zero Local Remittance, §6.9.14's Commercial-Use Ceiling, §6.9.15's suspension of entity operation while zero jurisdictions are TRUE, §6.9.16's Parent–Child Reciprocity Program, §6.9.17's Gate, or §6.9.19's Asymmetric Default: no AGPL, no CC BY-SA, and no L1–L3 rung stands in for those structural conditions — see §6.9.7. An entity barred by §6.9.15(a) does not fall back to AGPL or CC BY-SA either: those are still grants an entity would be exercising, and §6.9.15(a) reaches the entity's right to operate at all, not merely the primary SVE grant's terms. Those are not copyright mechanics with a swappable equivalent; a failure there is a termination or a relocation-and-transition duty, never a downgrade to a lesser license that would let the underlying problem continue under a different label.

### §13 — Ratchet & Retroactive Envelope
From the Effective Date (§0.1) — not the earlier date of signature — v6.0 applies retroactively to all SVE-licensed works, all prior versions (including v5.5), and the entire Prior-Art registry — as a strengthening only: no right already granted is diminished, nothing already open is closed. Between signature and the Effective Date, v5.5 continues to govern exactly as §0.1 sets out, precisely so that nothing is retroactively disturbed before anyone has had the comment window §0.1 describes. Future minor versions may issue on the same §0 terms until a Veche ratifies canonically; future major versions may only strengthen §§0–12 — exactly as v6.0 itself does relative to v5.5, elevating §2 without narrowing anything.

### §14 — Severability
An invalid provision is severed and the remainder enforced to the fullest extent possible. §0 (Fruits Test), the Core Principles of Meta-License v4.0, §1.2–§1.3 of this License (Latent Activation and its channel-independence corollary, restating Core Principle 4), §2.1–§2.4 of this License (the Natural-Person Rule, per §2.7), §4.7 of this License (No Secondary Secrecy, restating Core Principle 3, Zero Secrecy), §9.2–§9.3 of this License (Field-Notes Duty and Research Integrity, also restating Core Principle 3, Zero Secrecy), §6.1 of this License (Absolute Bars), §6.2–§6.5 of this License (Universal Access, restating Core Principle 2), §6.10–§6.11 of this License (the Golden Rule and Scarce Resource Allocation, which give operative content to the Fruits Test and Absolute Bars respectively and stand on the same footing as the provisions they specify), and §6.9 of this License (Constitutional Equality Assurance, including §6.9.5's No Local Presence, §6.9.6's Zero Local Remittance, §6.9.14's Commercial-Use Ceiling, §6.9.15's suspension of entity operation while zero jurisdictions are TRUE, §6.9.16's Parent–Child Reciprocity Program, §6.9.17's Gate, and §6.9.19's Asymmetric Default, per §6.9.12) are **non-severable**: if any is held unenforceable in a given jurisdiction, the remainder is interpreted to maximize alignment with it rather than narrowed around it; only if that is impossible does this License become void in that jurisdiction — never silently cut down to a lesser rule. §0.2's standalone-validity principle (including its moral-rights fork) and §0.3's Contribution Rule are themselves structural rather than substantive protections and are treated as inseverable from this License's basic operation — a License that could be argued out of its own standalone-validity clause would lose the very protection that clause exists to provide. §9.1, §9.4–§9.6 (the Research/Truth-Bearer track's scope and safeguards) remain severable on ordinary terms unless a future version elevates them — see the open questions in the drafting notes; **§2 no longer is, as of v6.0.**

